<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<div id="p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="p2.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center"><span id="p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Supplement to “Activation Steering with a Feedback Controller”</span></p>
</div>
<div id="p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Table of Contents</span></p>
</div><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:100%;height:1px;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:100%;height:1px;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Related Works</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Recent works increasingly frame large language models (LLMs) as <em id="A1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">dynamical systems</em>, where
generation is a trajectory in latent space. This view shifts activation steering from heuristic nudging
to principled <em id="A1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">control</em>: rather than biasing outputs without guarantees, controllers enforce
constraints on trajectories with formal assurances <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">Cheng &amp; Amo Alonso, 2024</a>)</cite>. In our PID-steering
framework, this distinction is key: we treat the model as a plant with hidden states evolving under
controlled interventions.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Controllability of LLMs.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib46" title="" class="ltx_ref">Soatto et al. (2023)</a></cite> model decoder-only LLMs as discrete-time stochastic systems and prove
that, under idealized assumptions (Euclidean embeddings, well-trained semantics), they are
controllable in the space of meanings. This establishes that any semantic state is theoretically
reachable, but probabilities may be negligible in practice, and emergent behaviors like chain-of-thought
are not captured. Their results highlight both opportunities and risks: controllability opens adversarial
attack surfaces but also suggests defensive controllers.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Prompting as open-loop control.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">Luo et al. (2023)</a></cite> recast multi-round prompt engineering as an optimal control problem, where
each prompt is a control input maximizing task reward. This provides a unifying formalism for prompt
strategies, akin to open-loop control. Yet, the framework remains conceptual: metrics in discrete
language space are poorly defined, and no guarantees of stability or convergence are provided.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Closed-loop activation control.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">Cheng &amp; Amo Alonso (2024)</a></cite> propose <em id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Linear Semantic Control</em> (LiSeCo), which projects activations
into safe subspaces at each decoding step via a closed-form controller. This yields lightweight,
guaranteed control of simple attributes (e.g., toxicity, sentiment). However, the linearity assumption
only approximates LLM embeddings, guarantees are local rather than global, and long-horizon stability
remains unaddressed.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Dynamic representation editing.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kong et al. (2024)</a></cite> introduce <em id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">RE-CONTROL</em>, which learns a value function on hidden
states and applies gradient-based interventions at test time. This dynamic approach generalizes
steering into a Bellman-optimal control problem, balancing alignment with fluency. Still, accuracy of
the learned value function is critical, test-time optimization adds overhead, and local interventions
may not guarantee global alignment.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Together, these works move activation steering from heuristics to control theory. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib46" title="" class="ltx_ref">Soatto et al. (2023)</a></cite> prove fundamental controllability (but under strong assumptions), Luo et al. unify prompt strategies as open-loop control (without guarantees), <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">Cheng &amp; Amo Alonso (2024)</a></cite> derive closed-form activation control (limited to linear approximations), and <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kong et al. (2024)</a></cite> extend to dynamic optimal control (with overhead and approximation risks).</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Theoretical Proofs</h2>

<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Discretized PID controller</h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Implementing a continuous-time controller on digital hardware, such as PID, requires discretizing its derivative and integral terms <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">Åström &amp; Hägglund, 1995a</a>, p.95)</cite>
See <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1 (Discretizing PID steering vector) ‣ 3.2.2 Computing the Steering Direction Using a PID Feedback Controller ‣ 3.2 Proportional–Integral–Derivative (PID) Steering ‣ 3 Steering with a Feedback Controller ‣ Activation Steering with a Feedback Controller" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>
<span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof.</span>
We follow the discretization procedure for PID controllers in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">(<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">Åström &amp; Hägglund, 1995a</a>, Sec. 3.6, Ch. 3)</cite>.
For simplicity, the sampling period is normalized to <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h=1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A2.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Proportional term in Eqn. <a href="#S3.E15" title="In 3.2.2 Computing the Steering Direction Using a PID Feedback Controller ‣ 3.2 Proportional–Integral–Derivative (PID) Steering ‣ 3 Steering with a Feedback Controller ‣ Activation Steering with a Feedback Controller" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>.</em></p>
<table id="A2.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(t)={\bm{K}}_{p}\,{\bm{r}}(t)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑲</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒓</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(t)={\bm{K}}_{p}\,{\bm{r}}(t).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">The discrete-time form is obtained by substituting sampled variables for their continuous counterparts:</p>
<table id="A2.E21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(k)={\bm{K}}_{p}\,{\bm{r}}(k)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑲</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒓</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(k)={\bm{K}}_{p}\,{\bm{r}}(k).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A2.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Integral term in Eqn. <a href="#S3.E15" title="In 3.2.2 Computing the Steering Direction Using a PID Feedback Controller ‣ 3.2 Proportional–Integral–Derivative (PID) Steering ‣ 3 Steering with a Feedback Controller ‣ Activation Steering with a Feedback Controller" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>.</em></p>
<table id="A2.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(t)={\bm{K}}_{i}\int_{0}^{t}{\bm{r}}(\tau)\,d\tau\qquad\Rightarrow\qquad\frac{dI}{dt}={\bm{K}}_{i}\,{\bm{r}}(t)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑲</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi>𝒓</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mo stretchy="false">⇒</mo><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑲</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒓</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(t)={\bm{K}}_{i}\int_{0}^{t}{\bm{r}}(\tau)\,d\tau\qquad\Rightarrow\qquad\frac{dI}{dt}={\bm{K}}_{i}\,{\bm{r}}(t).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Using forward Euler with <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h=1</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A2.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(k+1)-I(k)={\bm{K}}_{i}\,{\bm{r}}(k)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑲</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒓</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(k+1)-I(k)={\bm{K}}_{i}\,{\bm{r}}(k).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p3.3" class="ltx_p">Hence</p>
<table id="A2.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(k+1)=I(k)+{\bm{K}}_{i}\,{\bm{r}}(k)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑲</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒓</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(k+1)=I(k)+{\bm{K}}_{i}\,{\bm{r}}(k),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p3.4" class="ltx_p">which is equivalent to</p>
<table id="A2.E22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(k)=I(0)+{\bm{K}}_{i}\sum_{j=0}^{k-1}{\bm{r}}(j)={\bm{K}}_{i}\sum_{j=0}^{k-1}{\bm{r}}(j)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑲</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><mi>𝒓</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑲</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><mi>𝒓</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(k)=I(0)+{\bm{K}}_{i}\sum_{j=0}^{k-1}{\bm{r}}(j)={\bm{K}}_{i}\sum_{j=0}^{k-1}{\bm{r}}(j),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p3.5" class="ltx_p">since <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I(0)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(0)=0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A2.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Derivative term in Eqn. <a href="#S3.E15" title="In 3.2.2 Computing the Steering Direction Using a PID Feedback Controller ‣ 3.2 Proportional–Integral–Derivative (PID) Steering ‣ 3 Steering with a Feedback Controller ‣ Activation Steering with a Feedback Controller" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>.</em></p>
<table id="A2.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D(t)={\bm{K}}_{d}\,\frac{d{\bm{r}}(t)}{dt}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑲</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒓</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D(t)={\bm{K}}_{d}\,\frac{d{\bm{r}}(t)}{dt}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p4.2" class="ltx_p">Approximating the derivative by the backward Euler difference with <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h=1</annotation></semantics></math> gives</p>
<table id="A2.E23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D(k)={\bm{K}}_{d}\,\big({\bm{r}}(k)-{\bm{r}}(k-1)\big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑲</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝒓</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝒓</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D(k)={\bm{K}}_{d}\,\big({\bm{r}}(k)-{\bm{r}}(k-1)\big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Combining equation <a href="#A2.E21" title="In B.1 Discretized PID controller ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Proofs ‣ Activation Steering with a Feedback Controller" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">21</span></a>, equation <a href="#A2.E22" title="In B.1 Discretized PID controller ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Proofs ‣ Activation Steering with a Feedback Controller" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">22</span></a>, and equation <a href="#A2.E23" title="In B.1 Discretized PID controller ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Proofs ‣ Activation Steering with a Feedback Controller" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">23</span></a> yields</p>
<table id="A2.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{u}}(k)={\bm{K}}_{p}\,{\bm{r}}(k)\;+\;{\bm{K}}_{i}\sum_{j=0}^{k-1}{\bm{r}}(j)\;+\;{\bm{K}}_{d}\big({\bm{r}}(k)-{\bm{r}}(k-1)\big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝒖</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑲</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒓</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑲</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><mi>𝒓</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑲</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝒓</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝒓</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{u}}(k)={\bm{K}}_{p}\,{\bm{r}}(k)\;+\;{\bm{K}}_{i}\sum_{j=0}^{k-1}{\bm{r}}(j)\;+\;{\bm{K}}_{d}\big({\bm{r}}(k)-{\bm{r}}(k-1)\big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\square" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\square</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Background on Input-to-state Stability &amp; Notations </h3>

<section id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Background on Input-to-state Stability (ISS)</h5>

<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In our proofs, the input-to-state stability (ISS) of a system can be established either through the definition of an ISS system in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">Jiang et al., 1999</a>, Def. 2.1)</cite> or via the use of an ISS-Lyapunov function as in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">Jiang et al., 1999</a>, Def. 2.2, Prop. 2.3)</cite>. We also rely on the definition of a Lyapunov function and the difference Lyapunov equation for linear discrete-time homogeneous dynamical systems in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gajic &amp; Qureshi, 2008</a>, Ch. 1, p. 8)</cite>. The existence of a solution to the Lyapunov equation, together with its bound, is stated in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gajic &amp; Qureshi, 2008</a>, Ch. 4, p. 110)</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For reference, we briefly note that input-to-state stability (ISS) extends the classical notion of Lyapunov by explicitly accounting for external inputs: the state remains bounded and eventually whenever the input is bounded. A Lyapunov function provides an energy-like certificate for stability, while the associated Lyapunov equation offers a constructive method for obtaining such functions in linear settings. These notions are central for analyzing stability and will be used throughout our proofs.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Conventions and assumptions (used throughout).</h5>

<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\|\cdot\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\cdot\|</annotation></semantics></math> denote the Euclidean norm on <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>; for a matrix <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> we also write <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|M\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|M\|</annotation></semantics></math> for the operator norm induced by the Euclidean norm, i.e.
<math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|M\|\;:=\;\sup_{\|x\|=1}\|Mx\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>M</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|M\|\;:=\;\sup_{\|x\|=1}\|Mx\|</annotation></semantics></math> (the spectral norm) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">Horn &amp; Johnson, 2012</a>, pp. 343–346)</cite>.
We assume (i) <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup_{k}\|\bar{{\bm{A}}}(k)\|&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>sup</mo><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{k}\|\bar{{\bm{A}}}(k)\|&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math>; (ii) <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{w}}(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒘</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{w}}(k)</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded (for a signal <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{w}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒘</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{w}}</annotation></semantics></math> we set <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|{\bm{w}}\|_{\infty}:=\sup_{k\geq 0}\|{\bm{w}}(k)\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">:=</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝒘</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|{\bm{w}}\|_{\infty}:=\sup_{k\geq 0}\|{\bm{w}}(k)\|</annotation></semantics></math>) ;
(iii) the controller gains are static and time-invariant scalar multiples of the identity.
We use the standard meaning of the classes <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{K}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{K}\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{K}\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math> as in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">Jiang et al., 1999</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.3 </span>Dynamics of the Average Error Across Layers</h3>

<div id="A2.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To formalize the problem setup, we consider <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> pairs of contrastive prompt/input tokens <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{({\bm{q}}^{+}_{i},{\bm{q}}^{-}_{i})\}_{i=1}^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒒</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒒</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{({\bm{q}}^{+}_{i},{\bm{q}}^{-}_{i})\}_{i=1}^{N}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{q}}^{+}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝒒</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{q}}^{+}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> carries the desired property and <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{q}}^{-}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝒒</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{q}}^{-}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> represents the opposite. For discrete time (layer) <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}_{i}^{\pm}(k)\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>±</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}_{i}^{\pm}(k)\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the corresponding activation vectors. The layer-to-layer evolution is</p>
<table id="A2.E24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E24.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\bm{x}}_{i}(k+1)\;=\;f_{i}^{(k)}\!\big({\bm{x}}(k)\big),\,\,\,i=1,\dots,N," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.677em">,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}_{i}(k+1)\;=\;f_{i}^{(k)}\!\big({\bm{x}}(k)\big),\,\,\,i=1,\dots,N,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">with <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{i}^{(k)}:\mathbb{R}^{d}\!\to\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{i}^{(k)}:\mathbb{R}^{d}\!\to\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> differentiable on the operating region. A steering input <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u(t)</annotation></semantics></math> is applied on the undesired branch:</p>
<table id="A2.E25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}_{i}^{-}(k+1)\;=\;f^{(k)}_{i}\!\big({\bm{x}}_{i}^{-}(k)+{\bm{u}}(k)\big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>𝒖</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}_{i}^{-}(k+1)\;=\;f^{(k)}_{i}\!\big({\bm{x}}_{i}^{-}(k)+{\bm{u}}(k)\big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(25)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Defining <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\bm{x}}^{\pm}(k):=\tfrac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}{\bm{x}}_{i}^{\pm}(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>±</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>±</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\bm{x}}^{\pm}(k):=\tfrac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}{\bm{x}}_{i}^{\pm}(k)</annotation></semantics></math>, we track the per-pair and average errors as</p>
<table id="A2.E26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{e}}_{i}(k):={\bm{x}}_{i}^{+}(k)-{\bm{x}}_{i}^{-}(k),\qquad\bar{\bm{e}}(k):=\bar{\bm{x}}^{+}(k)-\bar{\bm{x}}^{-}(k),\qquad\tilde{{\bm{e}}}_{i}(k)={\bm{e}}_{i}(k)-\bar{{\bm{e}}}(k)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒆</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒆</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒆</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{e}}_{i}(k):={\bm{x}}_{i}^{+}(k)-{\bm{x}}_{i}^{-}(k),\qquad\bar{\bm{e}}(k):=\bar{\bm{x}}^{+}(k)-\bar{\bm{x}}^{-}(k),\qquad\tilde{{\bm{e}}}_{i}(k)={\bm{e}}_{i}(k)-\bar{{\bm{e}}}(k).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Furthermore, we define <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{A}}_{i}(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{A}}_{i}(k)</annotation></semantics></math> as the Jacobian of <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{i}^{(k)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{i}^{(k)}</annotation></semantics></math> at <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}_{i}^{+}(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}_{i}^{+}(k)</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\bm{A}}_{i}(k):=J_{f_{i}^{(k)}}\!\big({\bm{x}}_{i}^{+}(k)\big),\qquad\bar{\bm{A}}(t):=\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}{\bm{A}}_{i}(k),\qquad\tilde{{\bm{A}}}_{i}(k)={\bm{A}}_{i}(k)-\bar{{\bm{A}}}(k)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\bm{A}}_{i}(k):=J_{f_{i}^{(k)}}\!\big({\bm{x}}_{i}^{+}(k)\big),\qquad\bar{\bm{A}}(t):=\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}{\bm{A}}_{i}(k),\qquad\tilde{{\bm{A}}}_{i}(k)={\bm{A}}_{i}(k)-\bar{{\bm{A}}}(k).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The dynamic of the average error <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{{\bm{e}}}(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒆</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{{\bm{e}}}(k)</annotation></semantics></math> is then given by Proposition <a href="#Thmproposition2" title="Proposition 2 (Error dynamics of activation steering) ‣ 4.1 Dynamics of the Average Error Across Layers ‣ 4 Theoretical Analysis of PID Steering ‣ Activation Steering with a Feedback Controller" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">See <a href="#Thmproposition2" title="Proposition 2 (Error dynamics of activation steering) ‣ 4.1 Dynamics of the Average Error Across Layers ‣ 4 Theoretical Analysis of PID Steering ‣ Activation Steering with a Feedback Controller" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>
<span id="A2.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof.</span>
The evolution of the average error <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\bm{e}}(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒆</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\bm{e}}(k)</annotation></semantics></math> through layers can be described as follows:</p>
<table id="A2.E28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\bm{e}}(k+1)=\bar{\bm{x}}^{+}(k+1)-\bar{\bm{x}}^{-}(k+1)=\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\!\Big[f^{(k)}_{i}\!\big({\bm{x}}_{i}^{+}(k)\big)-f^{(k)}_{i}\!\big({\bm{x}}_{i}^{-}(k)+{\bm{u}}(k)\big)\Big]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒆</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>𝒖</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\bm{e}}(k+1)=\bar{\bm{x}}^{+}(k+1)-\bar{\bm{x}}^{-}(k+1)=\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\!\Big[f^{(k)}_{i}\!\big({\bm{x}}_{i}^{+}(k)\big)-f^{(k)}_{i}\!\big({\bm{x}}_{i}^{-}(k)+{\bm{u}}(k)\big)\Big].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(28)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Linearizing <math id="A2.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{(k)}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{(k)}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> around <math id="A2.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}_{i}^{+}(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}_{i}^{+}(k)</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain</p>
<table id="A2.E29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{(k)}_{i}\big({\bm{x}}_{i}^{+}(k)+\delta\big)\approx f^{(k)}_{i}\big({\bm{x}}_{i}^{+}(k)\big)+J_{f^{(k)}_{i}}\big({\bm{x}}_{i}^{+}(k)\big)\cdot\delta," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{(k)}_{i}\big({\bm{x}}_{i}^{+}(k)+\delta\big)\approx f^{(k)}_{i}\big({\bm{x}}_{i}^{+}(k)\big)+J_{f^{(k)}_{i}}\big({\bm{x}}_{i}^{+}(k)\big)\cdot\delta,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(29)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p4.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{f^{(k)}_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>J</mi><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{f^{(k)}_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the Jacobian of <math id="A2.SS3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{(k)}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{(k)}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Setting <math id="A2.SS3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta=-\,{\bm{e}}_{i}(k)+{\bm{u}}(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>𝒖</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta=-\,{\bm{e}}_{i}(k)+{\bm{u}}(k)</annotation></semantics></math> yields</p>
<table id="A2.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{(k)}_{i}\big({\bm{x}}_{i}^{+}(k)+\delta\big)\approx f^{(k)}_{i}\big({\bm{x}}_{i}^{+}(k)\big)\;+\;{\bm{A}}_{i}(k)\,\big({\bm{e}}_{i}(k)+{\bm{u}}(k)\big)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>𝒖</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{(k)}_{i}\big({\bm{x}}_{i}^{+}(k)+\delta\big)\approx f^{(k)}_{i}\big({\bm{x}}_{i}^{+}(k)\big)\;+\;{\bm{A}}_{i}(k)\,\big({\bm{e}}_{i}(k)+{\bm{u}}(k)\big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Insert this into Eqn.<a href="#A2.E28" title="In B.3 Dynamics of the Average Error Across Layers ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Proofs ‣ Activation Steering with a Feedback Controller" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">28</span></a> we obtain</p>
<table id="A2.E30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\bm{e}}(k+1)=\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}{\bm{A}}_{i}(k)\,{\bm{e}}_{i}(k)-\bar{{\bm{A}}}(k)\,{\bm{u}}(k)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒆</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒖</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\bm{e}}(k+1)=\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}{\bm{A}}_{i}(k)\,{\bm{e}}_{i}(k)-\bar{{\bm{A}}}(k)\,{\bm{u}}(k).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(30)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS3.p7.1" class="ltx_p">Recall that</p>
<table id="A2.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{e}}_{i}(k)=\bar{{\bm{e}}}(k)+\tilde{{\bm{e}}}_{(i)}(k),\ \text{then}\ \frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\tilde{{\bm{e}}}_{(i)}(k)=0," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒆</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒆</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>then</mtext><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒆</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{e}}_{i}(k)=\bar{{\bm{e}}}(k)+\tilde{{\bm{e}}}_{(i)}(k),\ \text{then}\ \frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\tilde{{\bm{e}}}_{(i)}(k)=0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p7.2" class="ltx_p">and</p>
<table id="A2.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{A}}_{(i)}(t)=\bar{{\bm{A}}}(k)+\tilde{{\bm{A}}}_{(i)}(k),\ \text{then}\ \frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\tilde{{\bm{A}}}_{(i)}(k)=0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>then</mtext><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{A}}_{(i)}(t)=\bar{{\bm{A}}}(k)+\tilde{{\bm{A}}}_{(i)}(k),\ \text{then}\ \frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\tilde{{\bm{A}}}_{(i)}(k)=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p7.3" class="ltx_p">Therefore,</p>
<table id="A2.E31" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A2.E31X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E31X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bar{\bm{e}}(k+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒆</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bar{\bm{e}}(k+1)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E31X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}{\bm{A}}_{i}(k)\,{\bm{e}}_{i}(k)-\bar{{\bm{A}}}(k)\,{\bm{u}}(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒖</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}{\bm{A}}_{i}(k)\,{\bm{e}}_{i}(k)-\bar{{\bm{A}}}(k)\,{\bm{u}}(k)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="3" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(31)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E31Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E31Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\bar{{\bm{A}}}(k)\,\bar{\bm{e}}_{i}(k)-\bar{{\bm{A}}}(k)\,{\bm{u}}(k)+\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\tilde{{\bm{e}}}_{(i)}(k)\tilde{{\bm{A}}}_{(i)}(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒆</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒖</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒆</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\bar{{\bm{A}}}(k)\,\bar{\bm{e}}_{i}(k)-\bar{{\bm{A}}}(k)\,{\bm{u}}(k)+\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\tilde{{\bm{e}}}_{(i)}(k)\tilde{{\bm{A}}}_{(i)}(k)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E31Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E31Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\underbrace{\bar{{\bm{A}}}(k)\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\tilde{{\bm{e}}}_{(i)}(k)+\bar{{\bm{e}}}(k)\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\tilde{{\bm{A}}}_{(i)}(k)}_{=0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒆</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒆</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\underbrace{\bar{{\bm{A}}}(k)\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\tilde{{\bm{e}}}_{(i)}(k)+\bar{{\bm{e}}}(k)\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\tilde{{\bm{A}}}_{(i)}(k)}_{=0}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p7.4" class="ltx_p">We then obtain the final state-space model for the dynamics of <math id="A2.SS3.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{e}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{e}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> as</p>
<table id="A2.E32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{{\bm{e}}}(k+1)=\bar{{\bm{A}}}(k)\,\bar{{\bm{e}}}(k)-\bar{{\bm{A}}}(k)\,{\bm{u}}(k)+{\bm{w}}(k)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒆</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒆</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒖</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>𝒘</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{{\bm{e}}}(k+1)=\bar{{\bm{A}}}(k)\,\bar{{\bm{e}}}(k)-\bar{{\bm{A}}}(k)\,{\bm{u}}(k)+{\bm{w}}(k),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(32)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p7.5" class="ltx_p">where</p>
<table id="A2.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{w}}(k)=\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\tilde{{\bm{A}}}_{i}(k)\,\tilde{{\bm{e}}}_{i}(k)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝒘</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒆</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{w}}(k)=\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\tilde{{\bm{A}}}_{i}(k)\,\tilde{{\bm{e}}}_{i}(k),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p7.6" class="ltx_p">which acts as a time-dependent exogeneous disturbance to the model  <math id="A2.SS3.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\square" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\square</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.4 </span>Proportional (P) Control</h3>

<div id="A2.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Consider proportional control with</p>
<table id="A2.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{u}}(k)=K_{P}\bar{{\bm{e}}}(k),\quad(K_{I}=K_{D}=0)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝒖</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒆</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{u}}(k)=K_{P}\bar{{\bm{e}}}(k),\quad(K_{I}=K_{D}=0).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The dynamics Eqn. <a href="#S4.E20" title="In Proposition 2 (Error dynamics of activation steering) ‣ 4.1 Dynamics of the Average Error Across Layers ‣ 4 Theoretical Analysis of PID Steering ‣ Activation Steering with a Feedback Controller" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">20</span></a> then become</p>
<table id="A2.E33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{{\bm{e}}}(k)=M_{P}(k)\bar{{\bm{e}}}(k)+{\bm{w}}(k)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒆</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒆</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>𝒘</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{{\bm{e}}}(k)=M_{P}(k)\bar{{\bm{e}}}(k)+{\bm{w}}(k),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(33)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{P}(k)=\bar{{\bm{A}}}(k)(I-K_{P})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>P</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{P}(k)=\bar{{\bm{A}}}(k)(I-K_{P})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">With a suitable choice of <math id="A2.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{P}</annotation></semantics></math>, the system can be made input-to-state stable (ISS); that is, there exist a <math id="A2.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{KL}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{KL}</annotation></semantics></math>-function <math id="A2.SS4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> and a <math id="A2.SS4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{K}</annotation></semantics></math>-function <math id="A2.SS4.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> such that, for all disturbance <math id="A2.SS4.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{w}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒘</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{w}}</annotation></semantics></math> with bounded sup norm and all initial states <math id="A2.SS4.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{{\bm{e}}}(0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒆</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{{\bm{e}}}(0)</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A2.E34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\bar{{\bm{e}}}(k)\|\ \leq\ \beta(\|\bar{{\bm{e}}}(0)\|,k)\ +\ \gamma(\|{\bm{w}}\|_{\infty}),\quad k\in\mathbb{Z}_{\geq 0}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒆</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒆</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.722em">+</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\bar{{\bm{e}}}(k)\|\ \leq\ \beta(\|\bar{{\bm{e}}}(0)\|,k)\ +\ \gamma(\|{\bm{w}}\|_{\infty}),\quad k\in\mathbb{Z}_{\geq 0},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(34)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.p2.2" class="ltx_p">see <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">(<a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">Jiang et al., 1999</a>, Def. 2.1)</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">In particular, the error decays from the
initial condition and remains bounded under bounded disturbances.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS4.p4.1" class="ltx_p">See <a href="#Thmproposition1" title="Proposition 1 (Steady-state error of P-control activation steering) ‣ 3.1 Activation Steering as a P Controller ‣ 3 Steering with a Feedback Controller ‣ Activation Steering with a Feedback Controller" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>
<span id="A2.SS4.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof.</span>
Assume <math id="A2.SS4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup_{k}\|\bar{{\bm{A}}}(k)\|\leq M&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>sup</mo><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>M</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{k}\|\bar{{\bm{A}}}(k)\|\leq M&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS4.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{P}=pI" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{P}=pI</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.SS4.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.
Since <math id="A2.SS4.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{P}(k)=\bar{{\bm{A}}}(k)(I-K_{P})=\bar{{\bm{A}}}(k)(1-p)I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>P</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{P}(k)=\bar{{\bm{A}}}(k)(I-K_{P})=\bar{{\bm{A}}}(k)(1-p)I</annotation></semantics></math>, by sub-multiplicative property of matrix norm we have</p>
<table id="A2.E35" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|M_{P}(t)\|\leq\|\bar{A}(t)\|\,\|(1-p)I\|\leq M|1-p|=:q." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">=</mo><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|M_{P}(t)\|\leq\|\bar{A}(t)\|\,\|(1-p)I\|\leq M|1-p|=:q.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(35)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.p4.2" class="ltx_p">For <math id="A2.SS4.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\in\big(1-\tfrac{1}{M},1+\tfrac{1}{M}\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>M</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>M</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\in\big(1-\tfrac{1}{M},1+\tfrac{1}{M}\big)</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A2.SS4.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS4.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Expanding recursively,</p>
<table id="A2.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\bar{{\bm{e}}}(k)=M_{P}(k-1)\cdots M_{P}(0)\bar{{\bm{e}}}(0)+\sum_{j=0}^{k-1}M_{P}(k-1)\cdots M_{P}(j+1)w(j)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒆</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒆</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>w</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{{\bm{e}}}(k)=M_{P}(k-1)\cdots M_{P}(0)\bar{{\bm{e}}}(0)+\sum_{j=0}^{k-1}M_{P}(k-1)\cdots M_{P}(j+1)w(j).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.p5.2" class="ltx_p">Hence,</p>
<table id="A2.E36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\bar{{\bm{e}}}(k)\|\leq q^{k}\|\bar{{\bm{e}}}(0)\|+\sum_{j=0}^{k-1}q^{k-1-j}\|w(j)\|\leq q^{k}\|\bar{e}(0)\|+\frac{1-q^{k}}{1-q}\|w\|_{\infty}\leq q^{k}\|\bar{e}(0)\|+\frac{1}{1-q}\|w\|_{\infty}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒆</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒆</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>e</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\bar{{\bm{e}}}(k)\|\leq q^{k}\|\bar{{\bm{e}}}(0)\|+\sum_{j=0}^{k-1}q^{k-1-j}\|w(j)\|\leq q^{k}\|\bar{e}(0)\|+\frac{1-q^{k}}{1-q}\|w\|_{\infty}\leq q^{k}\|\bar{e}(0)\|+\frac{1}{1-q}\|w\|_{\infty}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(36)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS4.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A2.SS4.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, we can set <math id="A2.SS4.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta(s,k)=q^{k}s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta(s,k)=q^{k}s</annotation></semantics></math>, which is a <math id="A2.SS4.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{K}\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{K}\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math>-function
(decaying to zero as <math id="A2.SS4.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>), and <math id="A2.SS4.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma(s)=\tfrac{1}{1-q}s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma(s)=\tfrac{1}{1-q}s</annotation></semantics></math>, which is a <math id="A2.SS4.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{K}</annotation></semantics></math>-function, satisfying Eqn. <a href="#A2.E34" title="In B.4 Proportional (P) Control ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Proofs ‣ Activation Steering with a Feedback Controller" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">34</span></a>.
Therefore, the system is ISS.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS4.p7.1" class="ltx_p">However, there exists a steady-state error due to the disturbance <math id="A2.SS4.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{w}}(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒘</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{w}}(k)</annotation></semantics></math>.
In the best case, when <math id="A2.SS4.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{{\bm{A}}}(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{{\bm{A}}}(k)</annotation></semantics></math> converges to <math id="A2.SS4.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{{\bm{A}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{{\bm{A}}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS4.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{w}}(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒘</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{w}}(k)</annotation></semantics></math> converges to <math id="A2.SS4.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{w}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒘</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{w}}</annotation></semantics></math>, the error <math id="A2.SS4.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{{\bm{e}}}(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒆</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{{\bm{e}}}(k)</annotation></semantics></math> eventually converges to a steady state given by</p>
<table id="A2.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{{\bm{e}}}_{ss}=(I-\bar{{\bm{A}}}(1-pI))^{-1}{\bm{w}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒆</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒘</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{{\bm{e}}}_{ss}=(I-\bar{{\bm{A}}}(1-pI))^{-1}{\bm{w}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.p7.2" class="ltx_p">Therefore, <math id="A2.SS4.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{{\bm{e}}}_{ss}\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒆</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{{\bm{e}}}_{ss}\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math> if <math id="A2.SS4.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{w}}\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒘</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{w}}\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math>.
 <math id="A2.SS4.p7.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\square" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\square</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
<div id="Thmremark1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmremark1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark 1</span></span><span id="Thmremark1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> (Convergence rate versus <math id="Thmremark1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{P}</annotation></semantics></math>.)</span></h6>
<div id="Thmremark1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmremark1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmremark1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">From Ineq. <a href="#A2.E36" title="In B.4 Proportional (P) Control ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Proofs ‣ Activation Steering with a Feedback Controller" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">36</span></a>, smaller <math id="Thmremark1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> yields faster convergence. Because</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q(p)=M|1-p|=\begin{cases}M(1-p),&amp;p\in\big(1-\tfrac{1}{M},\,1\big),\\[3.0pt]
M(p-1),&amp;p\in\big[1,\,1+\tfrac{1}{M}\big),\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>M</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn> 1</mn><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∈</mo><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn> 1</mn><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>M</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q(p)=M|1-p|=\begin{cases}M(1-p),&amp;p\in\big(1-\tfrac{1}{M},\,1\big),\\[3.0pt]
M(p-1),&amp;p\in\big[1,\,1+\tfrac{1}{M}\big),\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmremark1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmremark1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">we have <math id="Thmremark1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tfrac{d}{dp}q(p)=-M&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tfrac{d}{dp}q(p)=-M&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="Thmremark1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmremark1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tfrac{d}{dp}q(p)=M&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>M</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tfrac{d}{dp}q(p)=M&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="Thmremark1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore the contraction factor <math id="Thmremark1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q(p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q(p)</annotation></semantics></math> is minimized at</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{\star}=1\quad\Longrightarrow\quad q^{\star}=0," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{\star}=1\quad\Longrightarrow\quad q^{\star}=0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmremark1.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmremark1.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">and increases as <math id="Thmremark1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> moves away from <math id="Thmremark1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> within the admissible interval.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.5 </span>Proportional-Integral (PI) Control</h3>

<div id="A2.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To reduce the steady-state error, the proportional controller is extended with an integral action, resulting in a proportional-integral (PI) control law:</p>
<table id="A2.E37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E37.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\bm{u}}(k)=K_{p}\bar{{\bm{e}}}(k)+K_{I}{\bm{s}}(k),\qquad{\bm{s}}(k+1)={\bm{s}}(k)+\bar{{\bm{e}}}(k),\qquad(K_{D}=0)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒖</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒆</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒆</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{u}}(k)=K_{p}\bar{{\bm{e}}}(k)+K_{I}{\bm{s}}(k),\qquad{\bm{s}}(k+1)={\bm{s}}(k)+\bar{{\bm{e}}}(k),\qquad(K_{D}=0).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(37)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The dynamics Eqn. <a href="#S4.E20" title="In Proposition 2 (Error dynamics of activation steering) ‣ 4.1 Dynamics of the Average Error Across Layers ‣ 4 Theoretical Analysis of PID Steering ‣ Activation Steering with a Feedback Controller" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">20</span></a> then become</p>
<table id="A2.E38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{{\bm{e}}}(k+1)=\bar{{\bm{A}}}(k)(I-K_{P})\bar{{\bm{e}}}(k)-\bar{{\bm{A}}}(k)K_{I}{\bm{s}}(k)+{\bm{w}}(k)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒆</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>P</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒆</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>𝒘</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{{\bm{e}}}(k+1)=\bar{{\bm{A}}}(k)(I-K_{P})\bar{{\bm{e}}}(k)-\bar{{\bm{A}}}(k)K_{I}{\bm{s}}(k)+{\bm{w}}(k).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(38)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS5.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We use the following orthogonal decomposition for <math id="A2.SS5.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{w}}(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒘</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{w}}(k)</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{w}}(k)={\bm{w}}^{\parallel}(k)+{\bm{w}}^{\perp}(k)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝒘</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝒘</mi><mo>∥</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒘</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{w}}(k)={\bm{w}}^{\parallel}(k)+{\bm{w}}^{\perp}(k),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS5.p3.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS5.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{w}}^{\parallel}(k)\in\mathrm{Im}\,\bar{{\bm{A}}}(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝒘</mi><mo>∥</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{w}}^{\parallel}(k)\in\mathrm{Im}\,\bar{{\bm{A}}}(k)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS5.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{w}}^{\perp}(k)\in(\mathrm{Im}\,\bar{{\bm{A}}}(k))^{\perp}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝒘</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⟂</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{w}}^{\perp}(k)\in(\mathrm{Im}\,\bar{{\bm{A}}}(k))^{\perp}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS5.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The impact of <math id="A2.SS5.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{w}}^{\parallel}(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝒘</mi><mo>∥</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{w}}^{\parallel}(k)</annotation></semantics></math> on the error can be eliminated by PI control, as discussed below.
On the other hand, P-only control is not able to do so, because keeping <math id="A2.SS5.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{{\bm{e}}}(k)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒆</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{{\bm{e}}}(k)=0</annotation></semantics></math> requires <math id="A2.SS5.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{u}}(k)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝒖</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{u}}(k)=0</annotation></semantics></math>, leaving no component in <math id="A2.SS5.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{u}}(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒖</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{u}}(k)</annotation></semantics></math> that can compensate for <math id="A2.SS5.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{w}}^{\parallel}(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝒘</mi><mo>∥</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{w}}^{\parallel}(k)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS5.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A2.SS5.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{w}}^{\parallel}(k)\in\mathrm{Im}\,\bar{{\bm{A}}}(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝒘</mi><mo>∥</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{w}}^{\parallel}(k)\in\mathrm{Im}\,\bar{{\bm{A}}}(k)</annotation></semantics></math>, it can be expressed as</p>
<table id="A2.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\bm{w}}^{\parallel}(k)=\bar{{\bm{A}}}(k)K_{I}s^{*}(k).\quad\iff\quad{\bm{s}}^{*}(k)=K_{I}^{-1}\bar{{\bm{A}}}(k)^{\dagger}{\bm{w}}^{\parallel}(k)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝒘</mi><mo>∥</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">.</mo><mo lspace="0.0835em" stretchy="false">⇔</mo><msup><mi>𝒔</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>K</mi><mi>I</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup><msup><mi>𝒘</mi><mo>∥</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{w}}^{\parallel}(k)=\bar{{\bm{A}}}(k)K_{I}s^{*}(k).\quad\iff\quad{\bm{s}}^{*}(k)=K_{I}^{-1}\bar{{\bm{A}}}(k)^{\dagger}{\bm{w}}^{\parallel}(k)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS5.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A2.SS5.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{{\bm{s}}}(k)={\bm{s}}(k)-{\bm{s}}^{*}(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒔</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝒔</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒔</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{{\bm{s}}}(k)={\bm{s}}(k)-{\bm{s}}^{*}(k)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS5.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d(k)=s^{*}(k+1)-s^{*}(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d(k)=s^{*}(k+1)-s^{*}(k)</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore,</p>
<table id="A2.E39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{{\bm{s}}}(k+1)=\tilde{{\bm{s}}}(k)+\bar{{\bm{e}}}(k)-{\bm{d}}(k)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒔</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒔</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒆</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝒅</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{{\bm{s}}}(k+1)=\tilde{{\bm{s}}}(k)+\bar{{\bm{e}}}(k)-{\bm{d}}(k)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(39)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS5.p6.2" class="ltx_p">Insert <math id="A2.SS5.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{s}}(k)={\bm{s}}^{*}(k)+\tilde{{\bm{s}}}(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝒔</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝒔</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒔</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{s}}(k)={\bm{s}}^{*}(k)+\tilde{{\bm{s}}}(k)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS5.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{w}}(k)={\bm{w}}^{\parallel}(k)+{\bm{w}}^{\perp}(k)=\bar{{\bm{A}}}(k)K_{I}s^{*}(k)+{\bm{w}}^{\perp}(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝒘</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝒘</mi><mo>∥</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒘</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒘</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{w}}(k)={\bm{w}}^{\parallel}(k)+{\bm{w}}^{\perp}(k)=\bar{{\bm{A}}}(k)K_{I}s^{*}(k)+{\bm{w}}^{\perp}(k)</annotation></semantics></math> into Eqn. <a href="#A2.E38" title="In B.5 Proportional-Integral (PI) Control ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Proofs ‣ Activation Steering with a Feedback Controller" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">38</span></a>,</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A2.E40" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A2.E40X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E40X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bar{{\bm{e}}}(k+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒆</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bar{{\bm{e}}}(k+1)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E40X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\bar{{\bm{A}}}(k)(I-{\bm{K}}_{p})\bar{{\bm{e}}}(k)-\bar{{\bm{A}}}(k){\bm{K}}_{i}{\bm{s}}^{*}(k)-\bar{{\bm{A}}}(k){\bm{K}}_{i}\tilde{{\bm{s}}}(k)+\bar{{\bm{A}}}(k){\bm{K}}_{i}s^{*}(k)+{\bm{w}}^{\perp}(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝑲</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒆</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑲</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒔</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑲</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒔</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑲</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒘</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\bar{{\bm{A}}}(k)(I-{\bm{K}}_{p})\bar{{\bm{e}}}(k)-\bar{{\bm{A}}}(k){\bm{K}}_{i}{\bm{s}}^{*}(k)-\bar{{\bm{A}}}(k){\bm{K}}_{i}\tilde{{\bm{s}}}(k)+\bar{{\bm{A}}}(k){\bm{K}}_{i}s^{*}(k)+{\bm{w}}^{\perp}(k)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(40)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E40Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E40Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\bar{{\bm{A}}}(k)(I-{\bm{K}}_{p})\bar{{\bm{e}}}(k)-\bar{{\bm{A}}}(k){\bm{K}}_{i}\tilde{{\bm{s}}}(k)+{\bm{w}}^{\perp}(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝑲</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒆</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑲</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒔</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒘</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\bar{{\bm{A}}}(k)(I-{\bm{K}}_{p})\bar{{\bm{e}}}(k)-\bar{{\bm{A}}}(k){\bm{K}}_{i}\tilde{{\bm{s}}}(k)+{\bm{w}}^{\perp}(k)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS5.p8.1" class="ltx_p">We introduce the lifted state <math id="A2.SS5.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k)=\begin{bmatrix}\bar{{\bm{e}}}(k)\\[2.0pt]
\tilde{{\bm{s}}}(k)\end{bmatrix}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ζ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>PI</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒆</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒔</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k)=\begin{bmatrix}\bar{{\bm{e}}}(k)\\[2.0pt]
\tilde{{\bm{s}}}(k)\end{bmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math> with its dynamic derived from Eqn. <a href="#A2.E39" title="In B.5 Proportional-Integral (PI) Control ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Proofs ‣ Activation Steering with a Feedback Controller" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">39</span></a>-<a href="#A2.E40" title="In B.5 Proportional-Integral (PI) Control ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Proofs ‣ Activation Steering with a Feedback Controller" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">40</span></a> as follow</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A2.E41" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k+1)\;=\;{\bm{M}}_{i}(t)\,\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k)\;+\;\tilde{{\bm{w}}}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ζ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>PI</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑴</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ζ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>PI</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒘</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>PI</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k+1)\;=\;{\bm{M}}_{i}(t)\,\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k)\;+\;\tilde{{\bm{w}}}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(41)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS5.p9.1" class="ltx_p">where</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A2.Ex23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{M}}_{i}(k)=\begin{bmatrix}{\bm{M}}_{p}(k)&amp;-\,{\bm{G}}(k)\\
I&amp;I\end{bmatrix}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑴</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>𝑴</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝑮</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>I</mi></mtd><mtd><mi>I</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{M}}_{i}(k)=\begin{bmatrix}{\bm{M}}_{p}(k)&amp;-\,{\bm{G}}(k)\\
I&amp;I\end{bmatrix},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS5.p10.1" class="ltx_p">with <math id="A2.SS5.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{M}}_{p}(k)=\bar{{\bm{A}}}(p)(I-{\bm{K}}_{p})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑴</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝑲</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{M}}_{p}(k)=\bar{{\bm{A}}}(p)(I-{\bm{K}}_{p})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS5.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{G}}(k)=\bar{{\bm{A}}}(k){\bm{K}}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑮</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑲</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{G}}(k)=\bar{{\bm{A}}}(k){\bm{K}}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>
and</p>
<table id="A2.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{{\bm{w}}}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k)=\begin{bmatrix}{\bm{w}}^{\perp}(k)\\[2.0pt]
-d(k)\end{bmatrix}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒘</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>PI</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msup><mi>𝒘</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{{\bm{w}}}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k)=\begin{bmatrix}{\bm{w}}^{\perp}(k)\\[2.0pt]
-d(k)\end{bmatrix},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.p11" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS5.p11.1" class="ltx_p">See <a href="#Thmproposition3" title="Proposition 3 (Stabilizing the PI loop reduces steady-state error) ‣ 4.2.1 PI Control ‣ 4.2 Stability of the Error Dynamics: Roles and Caveats of PI and PID Control ‣ 4 Theoretical Analysis of PID Steering ‣ Activation Steering with a Feedback Controller" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>
<span id="A2.SS5.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof.</span>
Using the sub-multiplicativity of the induced matrix norm and the triangle inequality, and noting that <math id="A2.SS5.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|{\bm{M}}_{p}(k)\|\leq q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑴</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|{\bm{M}}_{p}(k)\|\leq q</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS5.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|{\bm{G}}(k)\|=\|\bar{{\bm{A}}}(k){\bm{K}}_{i}\|\leq\|\bar{{\bm{A}}}(k)\|\,\|K_{I}\|\leq Mh" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝑮</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑲</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|{\bm{G}}(k)\|=\|\bar{{\bm{A}}}(k){\bm{K}}_{i}\|\leq\|\bar{{\bm{A}}}(k)\|\,\|K_{I}\|\leq Mh</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain</p>
<table id="A2.EGx18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|\bar{{\bm{e}}}(k+1)\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒆</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|\bar{{\bm{e}}}(k+1)\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex25.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\|{\bm{M}}_{p}(k)\|\,\|\bar{{\bm{e}}}(k)\|+\|{\bm{G}}(k)\|\,\|\tilde{{\bm{s}}}(k)\|+\|{\bm{w}}^{\perp}(k)\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑴</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒆</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑮</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒔</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">+</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒘</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\|{\bm{M}}_{p}(k)\|\,\|\bar{{\bm{e}}}(k)\|+\|{\bm{G}}(k)\|\,\|\tilde{{\bm{s}}}(k)\|+\|{\bm{w}}^{\perp}(k)\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E42"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq q\,\|\bar{{\bm{e}}}(k)\|+Mh\,\|\tilde{{\bm{s}}}(k)\|+\|{\bm{w}}^{\perp}(k)\|," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒆</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒔</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒘</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq q\,\|\bar{{\bm{e}}}(k)\|+Mh\,\|\tilde{{\bm{s}}}(k)\|+\|{\bm{w}}^{\perp}(k)\|,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(42)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E43"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|\tilde{{\bm{s}}}(k+1)\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒔</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|\tilde{{\bm{s}}}(k+1)\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E43.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\|\bar{{\bm{e}}}(k)\|+\|\tilde{{\bm{s}}}(k)\|+\|d(k)\|." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒆</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒔</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\|\bar{{\bm{e}}}(k)\|+\|\tilde{{\bm{s}}}(k)\|+\|d(k)\|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(43)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS5.p11.2" class="ltx_p">Introduce</p>
<table id="A2.Ex26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z(k):=\begin{bmatrix}\|\bar{{\bm{e}}}(k)\|\\[2.0pt]
\|\tilde{{\bm{s}}}(k)\|\end{bmatrix},\qquad H:=\begin{bmatrix}q&amp;Mh\\[2.0pt]
1&amp;1\end{bmatrix},\qquad v(k):=\begin{bmatrix}\|{\bm{w}}^{\perp}(k)\|\\[2.0pt]
\|d(k)\|\end{bmatrix}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒆</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒔</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mi>q</mi></mtd><mtd><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒘</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z(k):=\begin{bmatrix}\|\bar{{\bm{e}}}(k)\|\\[2.0pt]
\|\tilde{{\bm{s}}}(k)\|\end{bmatrix},\qquad H:=\begin{bmatrix}q&amp;Mh\\[2.0pt]
1&amp;1\end{bmatrix},\qquad v(k):=\begin{bmatrix}\|{\bm{w}}^{\perp}(k)\|\\[2.0pt]
\|d(k)\|\end{bmatrix}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS5.p11.3" class="ltx_p">Then Eqn. <a href="#A2.E42" title="In B.5 Proportional-Integral (PI) Control ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Proofs ‣ Activation Steering with a Feedback Controller" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">42</span></a>- <a href="#A2.E43" title="In B.5 Proportional-Integral (PI) Control ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Proofs ‣ Activation Steering with a Feedback Controller" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">43</span></a> give the comparison
system</p>
<table id="A2.E44" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z(k+1)\ \leq\ H\,z(k)+v(k)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z(k+1)\ \leq\ H\,z(k)+v(k).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(44)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS5.p11.4" class="ltx_p">Expanding Eqn. <a href="#A2.E44" title="In B.5 Proportional-Integral (PI) Control ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Proofs ‣ Activation Steering with a Feedback Controller" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">44</span></a> recursively yields</p>
<table id="A2.E45" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z(k)\ \leq\ H^{k}z(0)+\sum_{i=0}^{k-1}H^{\,k-1-i}v(i)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z(k)\ \leq\ H^{k}z(0)+\sum_{i=0}^{k-1}H^{\,k-1-i}v(i).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(45)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.p12" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS5.p12.1" class="ltx_p">Consider the characteristic equation of <math id="A2.SS5.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\lambda-q)(\lambda-1)-Mh=0\ \Longleftrightarrow\ \lambda^{2}-(q+1)\lambda+(q+Mh)=0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="0.778em" stretchy="false">⟺</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\lambda-q)(\lambda-1)-Mh=0\ \Longleftrightarrow\ \lambda^{2}-(q+1)\lambda+(q+Mh)=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS5.p12.2" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A2.SS5.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q+Mh&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q+Mh&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, the maximal root <math id="A2.SS5.p12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>λ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies
<math id="A2.SS5.p12.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda^{\star}&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda^{\star}&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, hence the spectral radius <math id="A2.SS5.p12.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho(H)&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho(H)&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.p13" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS5.p13.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A2.SS5.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r:=\rho(H)&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r:=\rho(H)&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math> be the spectral radius of <math id="A2.SS5.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math>.
By the Gelfand formula for induced (operator) norms,</p>
<table id="A2.Ex28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lim_{k\to\infty}\|H^{k}\|^{1/k}\;=\;r\qquad\text{\cite[citep]{(\@@bibref{AuthorsPhrase1Year}{horn2012matrix}{\@@citephrase{, }}{}, p.\penalty\ 349)}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><msup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mtext class="ltx_citemacro_citep"><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">Horn &amp; Johnson, 2012</a>, p. 349)</cite></mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lim_{k\to\infty}\|H^{k}\|^{1/k}\;=\;r\qquad\text{\cite[citep]{(\@@bibref{AuthorsPhrase1Year}{horn2012matrix}{\@@citephrase{, }}{}, p.\penalty\ 349)}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS5.p13.2" class="ltx_p">Fix any <math id="A2.SS5.p13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho\in(r,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho\in(r,1)</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, by the definition of the limit, there exists
<math id="A2.SS5.p13.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math> such that</p>
<table id="A2.Ex29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|H^{k}\|^{1/k}\;\leq\;\rho\quad\text{for all }k\geq N\;\;\Longrightarrow\;\;\|H^{k}\|\;\leq\;\rho^{k}\quad\forall\,k\geq N." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mtext>for all </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.838em" rspace="0.838em" stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow><mspace style="width:1.167em;" width="1.167em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">∀</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|H^{k}\|^{1/k}\;\leq\;\rho\quad\text{for all }k\geq N\;\;\Longrightarrow\;\;\|H^{k}\|\;\leq\;\rho^{k}\quad\forall\,k\geq N.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS5.p13.3" class="ltx_p">Define the constant</p>
<table id="A2.Ex30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\;:=\;\max\Big\{\,1,\ \max_{0\leq k\leq N}\,\|H^{k}\|\,\rho^{-k}\Big\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">:=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn> 1</mn><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\;:=\;\max\Big\{\,1,\ \max_{0\leq k\leq N}\,\|H^{k}\|\,\rho^{-k}\Big\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS5.p13.4" class="ltx_p">Then:</p>
<ul id="A2.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\geq N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\geq N</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|H^{k}\|\,\rho^{-k}\leq 1\leq C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|H^{k}\|\,\rho^{-k}\leq 1\leq C</annotation></semantics></math>, hence
<math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|H^{k}\|\leq C\,\rho^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|H^{k}\|\leq C\,\rho^{k}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq k\leq N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq k\leq N</annotation></semantics></math>, we have
<math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|H^{k}\|\,\rho^{-k}\leq\max_{0\leq k\leq N}\|H^{k}\|\,\rho^{-k}\leq C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|H^{k}\|\,\rho^{-k}\leq\max_{0\leq k\leq N}\|H^{k}\|\,\rho^{-k}\leq C</annotation></semantics></math>,
hence <math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|H^{k}\|\leq C\,\rho^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|H^{k}\|\leq C\,\rho^{k}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A2.SS5.p13.5" class="ltx_p">Therefore,</p>
<table id="A2.E46" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|H^{k}\|\;\leq\;C\,\rho^{k}\qquad\text{for all }k\geq 0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mtext>for all </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|H^{k}\|\;\leq\;C\,\rho^{k}\qquad\text{for all }k\geq 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(46)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.p14" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS5.p14.1" class="ltx_p">Applying Eqn. <a href="#A2.E46" title="In B.5 Proportional-Integral (PI) Control ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Proofs ‣ Activation Steering with a Feedback Controller" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">46</span></a> to Eqn. <a href="#A2.E45" title="In B.5 Proportional-Integral (PI) Control ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Proofs ‣ Activation Steering with a Feedback Controller" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">45</span></a> gives</p>
<table id="A2.EGx19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|z(k)\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|z(k)\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex31.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\|H^{k}\|\,\|z(0)\|+\sum_{i=0}^{k-1}\|H^{k-1-i}\|\,\|v(i)\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\|H^{k}\|\,\|z(0)\|+\sum_{i=0}^{k-1}\|H^{k-1-i}\|\,\|v(i)\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq C\rho^{k}\|z(0)\|+C\sum_{i=0}^{k-1}\rho^{k-1-i}\|v(i)\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq C\rho^{k}\|z(0)\|+C\sum_{i=0}^{k-1}\rho^{k-1-i}\|v(i)\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E47"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq C\rho^{k}\|z(0)\|+\frac{C}{1-\rho}\,\|v\|_{\infty}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>C</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq C\rho^{k}\|z(0)\|+\frac{C}{1-\rho}\,\|v\|_{\infty},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(47)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS5.p14.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS5.p14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|v\|_{\infty}:=\sup_{i\geq 0}\|v(i)\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">:=</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|v\|_{\infty}:=\sup_{i\geq 0}\|v(i)\|</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.p15" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS5.p15.1" class="ltx_p">By construction,</p>
<table id="A2.Ex33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\tilde{\zeta}_{\!PI}(k)\|=\Big\|\begin{bmatrix}\bar{{\bm{e}}}(k)\\
\tilde{{\bm{s}}}(k)\end{bmatrix}\Big\|=\big(\|\bar{{\bm{e}}}(k)\|^{2}+\|\tilde{{\bm{s}}}(k)\|^{2}\big)^{1/2}=\|z(k)\|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ζ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒆</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒔</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒆</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒔</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\tilde{\zeta}_{\!PI}(k)\|=\Big\|\begin{bmatrix}\bar{{\bm{e}}}(k)\\
\tilde{{\bm{s}}}(k)\end{bmatrix}\Big\|=\big(\|\bar{{\bm{e}}}(k)\|^{2}+\|\tilde{{\bm{s}}}(k)\|^{2}\big)^{1/2}=\|z(k)\|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS5.p15.2" class="ltx_p">Combining this identity with Eqn. <a href="#A2.E47" title="In B.5 Proportional-Integral (PI) Control ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Proofs ‣ Activation Steering with a Feedback Controller" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">47</span></a>, the ISS estimate follows with</p>
<table id="A2.Ex34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta(s,k):=C\rho^{k}\,s\ \in\ \mathcal{K}\mathcal{L},\qquad\gamma(s):=\frac{C}{1-\rho}\,s\ \in\ \mathcal{K}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="0.778em">∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>C</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="0.778em">∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta(s,k):=C\rho^{k}\,s\ \in\ \mathcal{K}\mathcal{L},\qquad\gamma(s):=\frac{C}{1-\rho}\,s\ \in\ \mathcal{K},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS5.p15.3" class="ltx_p">which proves that the PI closed loop Eqn. <a href="#A2.E41" title="In B.5 Proportional-Integral (PI) Control ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Proofs ‣ Activation Steering with a Feedback Controller" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">41</span></a> is ISS.  <math id="A2.SS5.p15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\square" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\square</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.p16" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS5.p16.1" class="ltx_p">The integral part exactly cancels the matched disturbance component <math id="A2.SS5.p16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{w}}^{\parallel}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝒘</mi><mo>∥</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{w}}^{\parallel}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The remaining error is due only to the unmatched component <math id="A2.SS5.p16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{w}}^{\perp}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝒘</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{w}}^{\perp}</annotation></semantics></math>, which cannot be compensated, and to the variation rate <math id="A2.SS5.p16.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d(k)</annotation></semantics></math> when <math id="A2.SS5.p16.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{{\bm{A}}}(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{{\bm{A}}}(k)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS5.p16.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{w}}(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒘</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{w}}(k)</annotation></semantics></math> change over time.
In the best scenario, if a steady state exists, i.e., <math id="A2.SS5.p16.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{{\bm{A}}}(k)\to\bar{{\bm{A}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{{\bm{A}}}(k)\to\bar{{\bm{A}}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS5.p16.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{w}}(k)\to{\bm{w}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝒘</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>𝒘</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{w}}(k)\to{\bm{w}}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.SS5.p16.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{w}}\in\mathrm{Im}\,\bar{{\bm{A}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒘</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>Im</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{w}}\in\mathrm{Im}\,\bar{{\bm{A}}}</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A2.SS5.p16.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{w}}^{\perp}\equiv 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝒘</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msup><mo>≡</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{w}}^{\perp}\equiv 0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS5.p16.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\equiv 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≡</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\equiv 0</annotation></semantics></math>, and thus <math id="A2.SS5.p16.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{{\bm{e}}}(k)\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒆</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{{\bm{e}}}(k)\to 0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmremark2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmremark2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark 2</span></span><span id="Thmremark2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> (Convergence rate versus <math id="Thmremark2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{K}}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{K}}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>)</span></h6>
<div id="Thmremark2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmremark2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmremark2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">From proposition <a href="#Thmproposition3" title="Proposition 3 (Stabilizing the PI loop reduces steady-state error) ‣ 4.2.1 PI Control ‣ 4.2 Stability of the Error Dynamics: Roles and Caveats of PI and PID Control ‣ 4 Theoretical Analysis of PID Steering ‣ Activation Steering with a Feedback Controller" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, the convergence rate of <math id="Thmremark2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\zeta}_{PI}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ζ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\zeta}_{PI}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> depends on <math id="Thmremark2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math>:
the smaller <math id="Thmremark2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math>, the faster the convergence. We also adopt the convention
(as in the proof) that <math id="Thmremark2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho\in(r,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho\in(r,1)</annotation></semantics></math>. Equivalently, we examined
<math id="Thmremark2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(h)=\rho(H)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(h)=\rho(H)</annotation></semantics></math> and proved that with <math id="Thmremark2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h=\frac{(1-q)^{2}}{4M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h=\frac{(1-q)^{2}}{4M}</annotation></semantics></math> this quantity is minimized.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.p17" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS5.p17.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS5.p17.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof</span>
Consider the characteristic polynomial of <math id="A2.SS5.p17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex35" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda^{2}-(q+1)\lambda+(q+Mh)=0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda^{2}-(q+1)\lambda+(q+Mh)=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS5.p17.2" class="ltx_p">Its discriminant is</p>
<table id="A2.Ex36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta(h)=(q+1)^{2}-4(q+Mh)=(q-1)^{2}-4Mh." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta(h)=(q+1)^{2}-4(q+Mh)=(q-1)^{2}-4Mh.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.p18" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS5.p18.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="A2.SS5.p18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta(h)\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta(h)\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> (i.e., <math id="A2.SS5.p18.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq h\leq\tfrac{(1-q)^{2}}{4M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq h\leq\tfrac{(1-q)^{2}}{4M}</annotation></semantics></math>), then</p>
<table id="A2.Ex37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(h)=\frac{q+1+\sqrt{\Delta(h)}}{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(h)=\frac{q+1+\sqrt{\Delta(h)}}{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS5.p18.2" class="ltx_p">and <math id="A2.SS5.p18.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(h)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(h)</annotation></semantics></math> decreases as <math id="A2.SS5.p18.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math> increases.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.p19" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS5.p19.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="A2.SS5.p19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta(h)&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta(h)&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math> (i.e., <math id="A2.SS5.p19.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tfrac{(1-q)^{2}}{4M}&lt;h&lt;\tfrac{1-q}{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>M</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tfrac{(1-q)^{2}}{4M}&lt;h&lt;\tfrac{1-q}{M}</annotation></semantics></math>), then</p>
<table id="A2.Ex38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(h)=\sqrt{q+Mh}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(h)=\sqrt{q+Mh},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS5.p19.2" class="ltx_p">and <math id="A2.SS5.p19.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(h)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(h)</annotation></semantics></math> decreases as <math id="A2.SS5.p19.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math> decreases.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.p20" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS5.p20.1" class="ltx_p">Hence <math id="A2.SS5.p20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(h)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(h)</annotation></semantics></math> can achieve its best (smallest) value at</p>
<table id="A2.E48" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h=\frac{(1-q)^{2}}{4M}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h=\frac{(1-q)^{2}}{4M},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(48)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.p21" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS5.p21.1" class="ltx_p">for which the error converges to zero the fastest.  <math id="A2.SS5.p21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\square" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\square</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS5.p22" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS5.p22.1" class="ltx_p">Nevertheless, as we discuss in the next section, in some situations such a large value of <math id="A2.SS5.p22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math>
may become a practical obstacle for PI control.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.6 </span>Oveshoot Mechanism</h3>

<section id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Phenomenon.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A common issue in standard PI settings is <em id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">overshooting</em>: the closed loop oscillates around the setpoint before settling (see <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">Åström &amp; Hägglund (1995a, Ch. 3, §3.3)</a></cite>). In our terms, the integral part accumulates past error and can push the output beyond the setpoint; subsequent sign changes of the error gradually “discharge” the integral, producing a decaying oscillation. The big overshoot is undesirable when we prefer a more stable response near zero. Below we analyze the same mechanism for our PI steering setting.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Citing an observation from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib54" title="" class="ltx_ref">Vu &amp; Nguyen (2025)</a></cite>: in the <em id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">absence</em> of
steering, the cosine similarity between error vectors at different layers is
consistently <em id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">positive</em>, i.e.,</p>
<table id="A2.Ex39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\cos\angle\!\big(\bar{{\bm{e}}}(i),\,\bar{{\bm{e}}}(j)\big)&gt;0\quad\text{for all layers }i,j," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.552em;" width="0.552em"><mi mathvariant="normal">∠</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒆</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒆</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mtext>for all layers </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\cos\angle\!\big(\bar{{\bm{e}}}(i),\,\bar{{\bm{e}}}(j)\big)&gt;0\quad\text{for all layers }i,j,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">so the layerwise errors share (approximately) the same direction.
Consequently, with <math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\bar{\bm{x}}^{+}(k)\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\bar{\bm{x}}^{+}(k)\}</annotation></semantics></math> serving as the trajectory setpoints and
<math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\bar{\bm{x}}^{-}(k)\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\bar{\bm{x}}^{-}(k)\}</annotation></semantics></math> the system output, an <em id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">overshoot event</em> occurs when
the instantaneous error reverses its initial orientation, namely when</p>
<table id="A2.Ex40" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle\bar{{\bm{e}}}(k),\,\bar{{\bm{e}}}(0)\rangle&lt;0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒆</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒆</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle\bar{{\bm{e}}}(k),\,\bar{{\bm{e}}}(0)\rangle&lt;0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p2.3" class="ltx_p">We now introduce the definitions used below.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Scalarization along a direction.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let</p>
<table id="A2.Ex41" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="v\;:=\;\frac{\bar{\bm{e}}(0)}{\|\bar{\bm{e}}(0)\|}\qquad\text{and project onto $v$:}\qquad{\bm{e}}_{v}(k):=v^{\top}\bar{\bm{e}}(k),\quad{\bm{s}}_{v}(k):=v^{\top}\tilde{\bm{s}}(k)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">:=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒆</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒆</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mfrac><mrow><mtext>and project onto </mtext><mi>v</mi><mtext>:</mtext></mrow><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒆</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒔</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\;:=\;\frac{\bar{\bm{e}}(0)}{\|\bar{\bm{e}}(0)\|}\qquad\text{and project onto $v$:}\qquad{\bm{e}}_{v}(k):=v^{\top}\bar{\bm{e}}(k),\quad{\bm{s}}_{v}(k):=v^{\top}\tilde{\bm{s}}(k).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">From the PI loop dynamics Eqn. <a href="#A2.E41" title="In B.5 Proportional-Integral (PI) Control ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Proofs ‣ Activation Steering with a Feedback Controller" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">41</span></a> we obtain the scalar PI pair</p>
<table id="A2.EGx20" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E49"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\bm{e}}_{v}(k+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\bm{e}}_{v}(k+1)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E49.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=a(k)\,{\bm{e}}_{v}(k)\ -\ b(k)\,{\bm{s}}_{v}(k)\ +\ {\bm{w}}_{v}^{\perp}(k)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.722em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.722em">+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>v</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=a(k)\,{\bm{e}}_{v}(k)\ -\ b(k)\,{\bm{s}}_{v}(k)\ +\ {\bm{w}}_{v}^{\perp}(k),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(49)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E50"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\bm{s}}_{v}(k+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\bm{s}}_{v}(k+1)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E50.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle={\bm{s}}_{v}(k)\ +\ {\bm{e}}_{v}(k)\ -\ d_{v}(k)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.722em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.722em">−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle={\bm{s}}_{v}(k)\ +\ {\bm{e}}_{v}(k)\ -\ d_{v}(k),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(50)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">with
<math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a(k)=v^{\top}\bar{\bm{A}}(k)(I-{\bm{K}}_{p})v=v^{\top}{\bm{M}}_{p}(k)v," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝑲</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑴</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a(k)=v^{\top}\bar{\bm{A}}(k)(I-{\bm{K}}_{p})v=v^{\top}{\bm{M}}_{p}(k)v,</annotation></semantics></math>
<math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b(k)=v^{\top}\bar{\bm{A}}(k){\bm{K}}_{i}v=v^{\top}G(k)v," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑲</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b(k)=v^{\top}\bar{\bm{A}}(k){\bm{K}}_{i}v=v^{\top}G(k)v,</annotation></semantics></math>
and projected disturbances
<math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{w}}_{v}^{\perp}(k):=v^{\top}{\bm{w}}^{\perp}(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>v</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒘</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{w}}_{v}^{\perp}(k):=v^{\top}{\bm{w}}^{\perp}(k)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{v}(k):=v^{\top}d(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{v}(k):=v^{\top}d(k)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Empirically (and consistently with the angular-steering observation in our setup), we have
<math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{\top}\bar{\bm{A}}(k)v\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{\top}\bar{\bm{A}}(k)v\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>; together with the gain <math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{K}}_{i}=hI" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑲</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{K}}_{i}=hI</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>,
this implies <math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b(k)\geq 0." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b(k)\geq 0.</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Also, the assumption <math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q:=\sup_{k}\|{\bm{M}}_{p}(k)\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo rspace="0.1389em">:=</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑴</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q:=\sup_{k}\|{\bm{M}}_{p}(k)\|</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M:=\sup_{k}\|\bar{\bm{A}}(k)\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo rspace="0.1389em">:=</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M:=\sup_{k}\|\bar{\bm{A}}(k)\|</annotation></semantics></math> yeilds</p>
<table id="A2.E51" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a(k)\leq q&lt;1,\qquad 0\leq b(k)\leq Mh," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a(k)\leq q&lt;1,\qquad 0\leq b(k)\leq Mh,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(51)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Since the system Eqn. <a href="#A2.E41" title="In B.5 Proportional-Integral (PI) Control ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Proofs ‣ Activation Steering with a Feedback Controller" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">41</span></a> is ISS, so is the system Eqn. <a href="#A2.E49" title="In Scalarization along a direction. ‣ B.6 Oveshoot Mechanism ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Proofs ‣ Activation Steering with a Feedback Controller" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">49</span></a>-Eqn. <a href="#A2.E50" title="In Scalarization along a direction. ‣ B.6 Oveshoot Mechanism ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Proofs ‣ Activation Steering with a Feedback Controller" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">50</span></a>.
In other words, both <math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{e}}_{v}(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{e}}_{v}(k)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{s}}_{v}(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{s}}_{v}(k)</annotation></semantics></math> decay.
Recall that</p>
<table id="A2.Ex42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{s}}_{v}(k)=\sum_{i=0}^{k-1}{\bm{e}}_{v}(i)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{s}}_{v}(k)=\sum_{i=0}^{k-1}{\bm{e}}_{v}(i).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p2.3" class="ltx_p">Hence, <math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{s}}_{v}(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{s}}_{v}(k)</annotation></semantics></math> can only decrease when <math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{e}}_{v}(k)&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{e}}_{v}(k)&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, which is precisely the moment when overshoot occurs. These overshooting and decaying phenomena are observed in empirical simulation, see Fig. <a href="#A2.F6" title="Figure 6 ‣ Scalarization along a direction. ‣ B.6 Oveshoot Mechanism ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Proofs ‣ Activation Steering with a Feedback Controller" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>. Below, we define the overshoot in our setting.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.F6" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A2.F6.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.04309v1/1p0_0p3_0p0llama_many_layers_esum.svg" id="A2.F6.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/411;" width="548" height="411"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(a) </span>PI</figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A2.F6.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.04309v1/1p0_0p3_0p01llama_many_layers_esum.svg" id="A2.F6.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/411;" width="548" height="411"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(b) </span>PID</figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 6: </span> Scalar errors across time step of randomly initialized model after applying PI and PID controller. Colors from blue to red denote the time (layer) dimension.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="Thmdefinition2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 2</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> (Overshoot and its amplitude)</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmdefinition2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">We say an <em id="Thmdefinition2.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">overshoot</em> occurs from time <math id="Thmdefinition2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{a}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="Thmdefinition2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{a}+m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{a}+m</annotation></semantics></math> if <math id="Thmdefinition2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{e}}_{v}(k)&lt;0\ \forall k=k_{a},k_{a}+1,...,k_{a}+m-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.667em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{e}}_{v}(k)&lt;0\ \forall k=k_{a},k_{a}+1,...,k_{a}+m-1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmdefinition2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{e}}_{v}(k)\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{e}}_{v}(k)\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="Thmdefinition2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=k_{a}-1,k_{a}+m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=k_{a}-1,k_{a}+m</annotation></semantics></math>. Its amplitude is defined as</span></p>
<table id="A2.E52" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{a}\ :=\ \max_{kt_{a}\leq i\leq k_{a}+m-1}\,|{\bm{e}}_{v}(i)|\ ." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="0.778em">:=</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{a}\ :=\ \max_{kt_{a}\leq i\leq k_{a}+m-1}\,|{\bm{e}}_{v}(i)|\ .</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(52)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">In standard PID settings illustrated in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">Åström &amp; Hägglund (1995a, Ch. 3, §3.3)</a></cite>), it is observed that the overshoot amplitude decays over time. This decay is also consistent with the ISS property of the closed loop: as both <math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{e}}_{v}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{e}}_{v}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{s}}_{v}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{s}}_{v}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> are driven down, subsequent oscillations tend to diminish in magnitude. In our simulation (see Fig. <a href="#A2.F6" title="Figure 6 ‣ Scalarization along a direction. ‣ B.6 Oveshoot Mechanism ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Proofs ‣ Activation Steering with a Feedback Controller" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>), the first overshoot appear to be representative. Hence, while we are not yet able to provide a formal proof, the empirical evidence and ISS intuition justify the first overshoot which is typically the dominant one and serves as a representative indicator of oscillatory behavior.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">This assumption is for Proposition <a href="#Thmproposition4" title="Proposition 4 (Agressive PI gain leads to a large first overshoot) ‣ Scalarization along a direction. ‣ B.6 Oveshoot Mechanism ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Proofs ‣ Activation Steering with a Feedback Controller" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>. Suppose that <math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a(t)\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a(t)\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>; equivalently, <math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p4.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p\in(1-\tfrac{1}{M},1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>M</mi></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\in(1-\tfrac{1}{M},1]</annotation></semantics></math>, which is the result of proposition <a href="#Thmproposition1" title="Proposition 1 (Steady-state error of P-control activation steering) ‣ 3.1 Activation Steering as a P Controller ‣ 3 Steering with a Feedback Controller ‣ Activation Steering with a Feedback Controller" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>. This assumption is expected to entail no loss of generality relative to the <math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|a(t)|\leq q&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|a(t)|\leq q&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math> assumption.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmproposition4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmproposition4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 4</span></span><span id="Thmproposition4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> (Agressive PI gain leads to a large first overshoot)</span></h6>
<div id="Thmproposition4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmproposition4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproposition4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmproposition4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> be the first sign-change time, i.e.,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex43" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{e}}_{\bm{v}}(j)\geq 0\ \ \forall\,j=0,1,\dots,k_{0}-1,\qquad{\bm{e}}_{\bm{v}}(k_{0})&lt;0," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>𝒗</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mspace style="width:1.167em;" width="1.167em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">∀</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>𝒗</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{e}}_{\bm{v}}(j)\geq 0\ \ \forall\,j=0,1,\dots,k_{0}-1,\qquad{\bm{e}}_{\bm{v}}(k_{0})&lt;0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmproposition4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproposition4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">and let <math id="Thmproposition4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> be the first time the trajectory returns to the nonnegative side,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex44" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\bm{e}}_{\bm{v}}(k_{1})\geq 0,\qquad{\bm{e}}_{\bm{v}}(i)&lt;0\ \ \forall\,i=k_{0},k_{0}+1,\dots,k_{1}-1." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>𝒗</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>𝒗</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.337em">∀</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{e}}_{\bm{v}}(k_{1})\geq 0,\qquad{\bm{e}}_{\bm{v}}(i)&lt;0\ \ \forall\,i=k_{0},k_{0}+1,\dots,k_{1}-1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmproposition4.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproposition4.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">As in Eqn.<a href="#A2.E52" title="In Definition 2 (Overshoot and its amplitude) ‣ Scalarization along a direction. ‣ B.6 Oveshoot Mechanism ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Proofs ‣ Activation Steering with a Feedback Controller" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">52</span></a>, the first overshoot amplitude is</span></p>
<table id="A2.E53" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{0}\ =\ \max_{k_{0}\leq i\leq k_{1}-1}\,|{\bm{e}}_{\bm{v}}(i)|\ =\ |{\bm{e}}_{\bm{v}}(i_{max})|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="0.778em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>𝒗</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>𝒗</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{0}\ =\ \max_{k_{0}\leq i\leq k_{1}-1}\,|{\bm{e}}_{\bm{v}}(i)|\ =\ |{\bm{e}}_{\bm{v}}(i_{max})|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(53)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmproposition4.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproposition4.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Assume <math id="Thmproposition4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup_{k}\|\bar{{\bm{A}}}(k)\|\leq M&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>sup</mo><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>M</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{k}\|\bar{{\bm{A}}}(k)\|\leq M&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="Thmproposition4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup_{k}\|{\bm{M}}_{p}(k)\|\leq q&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>sup</mo><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐌</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{k}\|{\bm{M}}_{p}(k)\|\leq q&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>. Denote <math id="Thmproposition4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|{\bm{K}}_{i}\|=:h." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝐊</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|{\bm{K}}_{i}\|=:h.</annotation></semantics></math>
and given <math id="Thmproposition4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q+Mh&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q+Mh&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>.
Therefore,</span></p>
<table id="A2.E54" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{0}\ \leq\ Mh\Big(\frac{1}{1-q}+\frac{1}{(1-q)^{2}}\Big)\,{\bm{e}}_{\bm{v}}(0)\ +\ \Big(\frac{Mh}{1-q}(k_{0}-1)+\frac{Mh}{1-q}\Big)\|{\bm{d}}\|_{\infty}+\frac{Mh(k_{0}-1)+1}{1-q}\|{\bm{w}}\|_{\infty};" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>𝒗</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.722em">+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒅</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.722em">+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>;</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{0}\ \leq\ Mh\Big(\frac{1}{1-q}+\frac{1}{(1-q)^{2}}\Big)\,{\bm{e}}_{\bm{v}}(0)\ +\ \Big(\frac{Mh}{1-q}(k_{0}-1)+\frac{Mh}{1-q}\Big)\|{\bm{d}}\|_{\infty}+\frac{Mh(k_{0}-1)+1}{1-q}\|{\bm{w}}\|_{\infty};</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(54)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof.</span>
Before the first crossing (<math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\leq k_{0}-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\leq k_{0}-1</annotation></semantics></math>) we have <math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{s}}_{v}(j)\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{s}}_{v}(j)\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, hence from
Eqn. <a href="#A2.E49" title="In Scalarization along a direction. ‣ B.6 Oveshoot Mechanism ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Proofs ‣ Activation Steering with a Feedback Controller" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">49</span></a></p>
<table id="A2.Ex45" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{e}}_{v}(j+1)=a(j){\bm{e}}_{v}(j)-b(j){\bm{s}}_{v}(j)+{\bm{w}}_{v}^{\perp}(j)\ \leq\ a(j){\bm{e}}_{v}(j)+{\bm{w}}_{v}^{\perp}(j)\ \leq\ q\,{\bm{e}}_{v}(j)+\|{\bm{w}}\|_{\infty}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>v</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>v</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{e}}_{v}(j+1)=a(j){\bm{e}}_{v}(j)-b(j){\bm{s}}_{v}(j)+{\bm{w}}_{v}^{\perp}(j)\ \leq\ a(j){\bm{e}}_{v}(j)+{\bm{w}}_{v}^{\perp}(j)\ \leq\ q\,{\bm{e}}_{v}(j)+\|{\bm{w}}\|_{\infty},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p5.2" class="ltx_p">so by induction <math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{e}}_{v}(j)\leq q^{j}{\bm{e}}_{v}(0)+\frac{1}{1-q}\|{\bm{w}}\|_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{e}}_{v}(j)\leq q^{j}{\bm{e}}_{v}(0)+\frac{1}{1-q}\|{\bm{w}}\|_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math>. Summing Eqn. <a href="#A2.E50" title="In Scalarization along a direction. ‣ B.6 Oveshoot Mechanism ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Proofs ‣ Activation Steering with a Feedback Controller" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">50</span></a>,</p>
<table id="A2.E55" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{s}}_{v}(k_{0}-1)\ =\ \sum_{i=0}^{k_{0}-2}{\bm{e}}_{v}(i)\ -\ \sum_{i=0}^{k_{0}-2}{\bm{d}}_{v}(i)\ \leq\ \frac{{\bm{e}}_{v}(0)}{1-q}\ +\ (k_{0}-1)\|{\bm{d}}\|_{\infty}+\ \frac{k_{0}-1}{1-q}\|{\bm{w}}\|_{\infty}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.611em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.555em">−</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>𝒅</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.722em" rspace="0.722em">+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒅</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.722em">+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{s}}_{v}(k_{0}-1)\ =\ \sum_{i=0}^{k_{0}-2}{\bm{e}}_{v}(i)\ -\ \sum_{i=0}^{k_{0}-2}{\bm{d}}_{v}(i)\ \leq\ \frac{{\bm{e}}_{v}(0)}{1-q}\ +\ (k_{0}-1)\|{\bm{d}}\|_{\infty}+\ \frac{k_{0}-1}{1-q}\|{\bm{w}}\|_{\infty}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(55)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p6.2" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a(k)\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a(k)\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{e}}_{v}(k_{0}-1)\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{e}}_{v}(k_{0}-1)\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, at the crossing step,</p>
<table id="A2.E56" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A2.E56X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E56X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle|{\bm{e}}_{v}(k_{0})|\ =\ -{\bm{e}}_{v}(k_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle|{\bm{e}}_{v}(k_{0})|\ =\ -{\bm{e}}_{v}(k_{0})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E56X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\ b(k_{0}-1)\,{\bm{s}}_{v}(k_{0}-1)\ +\ \|{\bm{w}}\|_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.722em">+</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\ b(k_{0}-1)\,{\bm{s}}_{v}(k_{0}-1)\ +\ \|{\bm{w}}\|_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="3" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(56)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E56Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E56Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\ Mh\!\left(\frac{{\bm{e}}_{v}(0)}{1-q}+(k_{0}-1)\|{\bm{d}}\|_{\infty}+\frac{k_{0}-1}{1-q}W_{\infty}\right)+\|{\bm{w}}\|_{\infty}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mpadded style="width:0.406em;" width="0.406em"><mi>h</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒅</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\ Mh\!\left(\frac{{\bm{e}}_{v}(0)}{1-q}+(k_{0}-1)\|{\bm{d}}\|_{\infty}+\frac{k_{0}-1}{1-q}W_{\infty}\right)+\|{\bm{w}}\|_{\infty}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E56Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E56Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{Mh}{1-q}{\bm{e}}_{v}(0)+Mh(k_{0}-1)\|{\bm{d}}\|_{\infty}+(Mh\frac{k_{0}-1}{1-q}+1)\|{\bm{w}}\|_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒅</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{Mh}{1-q}{\bm{e}}_{v}(0)+Mh(k_{0}-1)\|{\bm{d}}\|_{\infty}+(Mh\frac{k_{0}-1}{1-q}+1)\|{\bm{w}}\|_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p7.2" class="ltx_p">Assume that <math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{d}}_{v}(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒅</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{d}}_{v}(k)</annotation></semantics></math> is small enough s.t during the overshoot time, <math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{s}}_{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{s}}_{v}</annotation></semantics></math> is nonincreasing (since <math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{e}}_{v}&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{e}}_{v}&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math> a.e. on <math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[k_{0},k_{1}-1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[k_{0},k_{1}-1]</annotation></semantics></math>), so
<math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{s}}_{v}(i)\leq{\bm{s}}_{v}(k_{0}-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{s}}_{v}(i)\leq{\bm{s}}_{v}(k_{0}-1)</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[k_{0},k_{1}-1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[k_{0},k_{1}-1]</annotation></semantics></math>. Using Eqn. <a href="#A2.E49" title="In Scalarization along a direction. ‣ B.6 Oveshoot Mechanism ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Proofs ‣ Activation Steering with a Feedback Controller" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">49</span></a> again and
unrolling <math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> steps from <math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A2.E57" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A2.E57X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E57X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle|{\bm{e}}_{v}(k_{0}+m)|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle|{\bm{e}}_{v}(k_{0}+m)|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E57X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\ q^{m}|{\bm{e}}_{v}(k_{0})|\ +\ \sum_{k=0}^{m-1}q^{k}\big(Mh\,{\bm{s}}_{v}(k_{0}-1)+\|{\bm{w}}\|_{\infty}\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.722em">+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\ q^{m}|{\bm{e}}_{v}(k_{0})|\ +\ \sum_{k=0}^{m-1}q^{k}\big(Mh\,{\bm{s}}_{v}(k_{0}-1)+\|{\bm{w}}\|_{\infty}\big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(57)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E57Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E57Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\ |{\bm{e}}_{v}(k_{0})|\ +\ \frac{Mh\,{\bm{s}}_{v}(k_{0}-1)+\|{\bm{w}}\|_{\infty}}{1-q}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.722em">+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\ |{\bm{e}}_{v}(k_{0})|\ +\ \frac{Mh\,{\bm{s}}_{v}(k_{0}-1)+\|{\bm{w}}\|_{\infty}}{1-q}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p7.3" class="ltx_p">Taking the maximum over <math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p7.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\in\{0,1,\dots,k_{1}-k_{0}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\in\{0,1,\dots,k_{1}-k_{0}\}</annotation></semantics></math> and substituting Ineq. <a href="#A2.E55" title="In Scalarization along a direction. ‣ B.6 Oveshoot Mechanism ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Proofs ‣ Activation Steering with a Feedback Controller" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">55</span></a> and Ineq. <a href="#A2.E56" title="In Scalarization along a direction. ‣ B.6 Oveshoot Mechanism ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Proofs ‣ Activation Steering with a Feedback Controller" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">56</span></a> into Ineq. <a href="#A2.E57" title="In Scalarization along a direction. ‣ B.6 Oveshoot Mechanism ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Proofs ‣ Activation Steering with a Feedback Controller" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">57</span></a> yields</p>
<table id="A2.E58" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{0}\ \leq\ Mh\Big(\frac{1}{1-q}+\frac{1}{(1-q)^{2}}\Big)\,{\bm{e}}_{v}(0)\ +\ \Big(\frac{Mh}{1-q}(k_{0}-1)+\frac{Mh}{1-q}\Big)\|{\bm{d}}\|_{\infty}\ +\frac{Mh(k_{0}-1)+1}{1-q}\|{\bm{w}}\|_{\infty}\;" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.722em">+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒅</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.722em">+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{0}\ \leq\ Mh\Big(\frac{1}{1-q}+\frac{1}{(1-q)^{2}}\Big)\,{\bm{e}}_{v}(0)\ +\ \Big(\frac{Mh}{1-q}(k_{0}-1)+\frac{Mh}{1-q}\Big)\|{\bm{d}}\|_{\infty}\ +\frac{Mh(k_{0}-1)+1}{1-q}\|{\bm{w}}\|_{\infty}\;</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(58)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p7.4" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p7.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\square" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\square</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p8.1" class="ltx_p">Consequently, the right-hand side of Ineq.<a href="#A2.E58" title="In Scalarization along a direction. ‣ B.6 Oveshoot Mechanism ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Proofs ‣ Activation Steering with a Feedback Controller" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">58</span></a> is <em id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p8.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">monotone increasing in <math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math></em> (via the factor <math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Mh" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Mh</annotation></semantics></math>) and increases as <math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> decreases (through the factors <math id="A2.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{1-q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{1-q}</annotation></semantics></math>). In particular, more aggressive PI leads to a larger first–overshoot amplitude.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmremark3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmremark3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark 3</span></span><span id="Thmremark3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> (“Fast-PI” specialization.)</span></h6>
<div id="Thmremark3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmremark3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmremark3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">With the tuning used in our analysis in remark <a href="#Thmremark2" title="Remark 2 (Convergence rate versus 𝐾_𝑖) ‣ B.5 Proportional-Integral (PI) Control ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Proofs ‣ Activation Steering with a Feedback Controller" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, <math id="Thmremark3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h=\frac{(1-q)^{2}}{4M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h=\frac{(1-q)^{2}}{4M}</annotation></semantics></math> (the value that
minimizes the comparison-system rate), so <math id="Thmremark3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Mh=\frac{(1-q)^{2}}{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Mh=\frac{(1-q)^{2}}{4}</annotation></semantics></math>. Plugging into
equation <a href="#A2.E58" title="In Scalarization along a direction. ‣ B.6 Oveshoot Mechanism ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Proofs ‣ Activation Steering with a Feedback Controller" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">58</span></a> gives</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex46" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{A}}_{0}\ \leq\ \Big(\frac{1-q}{4}+\frac{1}{4}\Big)\,{\bm{e}}_{v}(0)\ +\ \Big(\frac{1-q}{4}(k_{0}-1)+\frac{1}{4}\Big)\|{\bm{d}}\|_{\infty}\ +\ \frac{k_{0}}{1-q}\|{\bm{w}}\|_{\infty}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.722em">+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒅</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.722em">+</mo><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{A}}_{0}\ \leq\ \Big(\frac{1-q}{4}+\frac{1}{4}\Big)\,{\bm{e}}_{v}(0)\ +\ \Big(\frac{1-q}{4}(k_{0}-1)+\frac{1}{4}\Big)\|{\bm{d}}\|_{\infty}\ +\ \frac{k_{0}}{1-q}\|{\bm{w}}\|_{\infty}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmremark3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmremark3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">In particular, in the disturbance-free case (<math id="Thmremark3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|{\bm{w}}\|_{\infty}=\|{\bm{d}}\|_{\infty}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐰</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐝</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|{\bm{w}}\|_{\infty}=\|{\bm{d}}\|_{\infty}=0</annotation></semantics></math>) we obtain</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex47" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{A}}_{0}\ \leq\ \Big(\frac{1-q}{4}+\frac{1}{4}\Big)\,{\bm{e}}_{v}(0)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{A}}_{0}\ \leq\ \Big(\frac{1-q}{4}+\frac{1}{4}\Big)\,{\bm{e}}_{v}(0),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmremark3.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmremark3.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">so stronger proportional action (smaller <math id="Thmremark3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>) comes with a larger first-overshoot
envelope, even though the closed-loop settles faster.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS7" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.7 </span>PID Control</h3>

<section id="A2.SS7.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">B.7.1 </span>Stability of PID closed loop</h4>

<div id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We consider the PID update</p>
<table id="A2.Ex48" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{u}}(k)\;=\;{\bm{K}}_{p}\,\bar{\bm{e}}(k)\;+\;{\bm{K}}_{i}\,{\bm{s}}(k)\;+\;{\bm{K}}_{d}\big(\bar{\bm{e}}(k)-\bar{\bm{e}}(k-1)\big)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝒖</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑲</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒆</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑲</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑲</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒆</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒆</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{u}}(k)\;=\;{\bm{K}}_{p}\,\bar{\bm{e}}(k)\;+\;{\bm{K}}_{i}\,{\bm{s}}(k)\;+\;{\bm{K}}_{d}\big(\bar{\bm{e}}(k)-\bar{\bm{e}}(k-1)\big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">and define the auxiliary matrices</p>
<table id="A2.Ex49" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{M}}_{p}(k):=\bar{\bm{A}}(k)\big(I-{\bm{K}}_{p}\big),\qquad{\bm{G}}(k):=\bar{\bm{A}}(k){\bm{K}}_{i},\qquad{\bm{H}}(k):=\bar{\bm{A}}(k){\bm{K}}_{d}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑴</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝑲</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑮</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑲</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑯</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑲</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{M}}_{p}(k):=\bar{\bm{A}}(k)\big(I-{\bm{K}}_{p}\big),\qquad{\bm{G}}(k):=\bar{\bm{A}}(k){\bm{K}}_{i},\qquad{\bm{H}}(k):=\bar{\bm{A}}(k){\bm{K}}_{d},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">together with the error increment</p>
<table id="A2.Ex50" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\bar{\bm{e}}(k):=\bar{\bm{e}}(k)-\bar{\bm{e}}(k-1),\qquad\Delta\bar{\bm{e}}(-1)=0" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒆</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒆</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒆</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒆</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\bar{\bm{e}}(k):=\bar{\bm{e}}(k)-\bar{\bm{e}}(k-1),\qquad\Delta\bar{\bm{e}}(-1)=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Using the plant relation, we obtain</p>
<table id="A2.E59" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E59.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\bar{\bm{e}}(k+1)\;=\;\big({\bm{M}}_{p}(k)-I\big)\bar{\bm{e}}(k)\;-\;{\bm{G}}(k)\tilde{{\bm{s}}}(k)\;-\;{\bm{H}}(k)\Delta\bar{\bm{e}}(k)\;+\;{\bm{w}}^{\perp}(k)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒆</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑴</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒆</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑮</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒔</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑯</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒆</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒘</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\bar{\bm{e}}(k+1)\;=\;\big({\bm{M}}_{p}(k)-I\big)\bar{\bm{e}}(k)\;-\;{\bm{G}}(k)\tilde{{\bm{s}}}(k)\;-\;{\bm{H}}(k)\Delta\bar{\bm{e}}(k)\;+\;{\bm{w}}^{\perp}(k),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(59)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Introduce the lifted state from the auxiliary PI state in Eqn. <a href="#A2.E41" title="In B.5 Proportional-Integral (PI) Control ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Proofs ‣ Activation Steering with a Feedback Controller" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">41</span></a></p>
<table id="A2.Ex51" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PID}}(k)\;:=\;\begin{bmatrix}\bar{\bm{e}}(k)\\[2.0pt]
\tilde{{\bm{s}}}(k)\\[2.0pt]
\Delta\bar{\bm{e}}(k)\end{bmatrix}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ζ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>PID</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">:=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒆</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒔</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒆</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PID}}(k)\;:=\;\begin{bmatrix}\bar{\bm{e}}(k)\\[2.0pt]
\tilde{{\bm{s}}}(k)\\[2.0pt]
\Delta\bar{\bm{e}}(k)\end{bmatrix},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Then the closed-loop evolution reads</p>
<table id="A2.E60" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PID}}(k+1)\;=\;{\bm{M}}_{d}(k)\,\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PID}}(k)\;+\;\tilde{\bm{w}}_{\mathrm{PID}}(k)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ζ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>PID</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑴</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ζ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>PID</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒘</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>PID</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PID}}(k+1)\;=\;{\bm{M}}_{d}(k)\,\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PID}}(k)\;+\;\tilde{\bm{w}}_{\mathrm{PID}}(k),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(60)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p2.3" class="ltx_p">where</p>
<table id="A2.Ex52" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{M}}_{d}(k)\;:=\;\begin{bmatrix}{\bm{M}}_{p}(k)&amp;-{\bm{G}}(k)&amp;-{\bm{H}}(k)\\
I&amp;I&amp;0\\
{\bm{M}}_{p}(k)-I&amp;-{\bm{G}}(k)&amp;-{\bm{H}}(k)\end{bmatrix},\qquad\tilde{{\bm{w}}}_{\mathrm{PID}}(k)\;:=\;\begin{bmatrix}{\bm{w}}^{\perp}(k)\\
-d(k)\\
{\bm{w}}^{\perp}(k)\end{bmatrix}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑴</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">:=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>𝑴</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝑮</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝑯</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>I</mi></mtd><mtd><mi>I</mi></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑴</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝑮</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝑯</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒘</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>PID</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">:=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msup><mi>𝒘</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msup><mi>𝒘</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{M}}_{d}(k)\;:=\;\begin{bmatrix}{\bm{M}}_{p}(k)&amp;-{\bm{G}}(k)&amp;-{\bm{H}}(k)\\
I&amp;I&amp;0\\
{\bm{M}}_{p}(k)-I&amp;-{\bm{G}}(k)&amp;-{\bm{H}}(k)\end{bmatrix},\qquad\tilde{{\bm{w}}}_{\mathrm{PID}}(k)\;:=\;\begin{bmatrix}{\bm{w}}^{\perp}(k)\\
-d(k)\\
{\bm{w}}^{\perp}(k)\end{bmatrix}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">See <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1 (Stabilizing the PID loop preserves bias removal) ‣ 4.2.2 PID Control ‣ 4.2 Stability of the Error Dynamics: Roles and Caveats of PI and PID Control ‣ 4 Theoretical Analysis of PID Steering ‣ Activation Steering with a Feedback Controller" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>
<span id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof.</span>
We establish the ISS for system <a href="#A2.E60" title="In B.7.1 Stability of PID closed loop ‣ B.7 PID Control ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Proofs ‣ Activation Steering with a Feedback Controller" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">60</span></a> using the method of ISS-Lyapunov function, see <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">Jiang et al., 1999</a>, Def. 2.2, Prop. 2.3)</cite>. It then suffices to construct a candidate ISS-Lyapunov function <math id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{V}}_{\mathrm{PID}}(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑽</mi><mi>PID</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{V}}_{\mathrm{PID}}(k)</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying that there exist class <math id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{K}_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{K}_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math> functions <math id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{1},\alpha_{2},\alpha_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{1},\alpha_{2},\alpha_{3}</annotation></semantics></math> and a class <math id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{K}</annotation></semantics></math> function <math id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math> such that</p>
<table id="A2.E61" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E61.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{1}(\|\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PID}}(k)\|)\;\leq\;{\bm{V}}_{\mathrm{PID}}(\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PID}}(k))\;\leq\;\alpha_{2}(\|\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PID}}(k)\|)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ζ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>PID</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑽</mi><mi>PID</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ζ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>PID</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ζ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>PID</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{1}(\|\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PID}}(k)\|)\;\leq\;{\bm{V}}_{\mathrm{PID}}(\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PID}}(k))\;\leq\;\alpha_{2}(\|\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PID}}(k)\|),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(61)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">and</p>
<table id="A2.E62" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E62.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{V}}(\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PID}}(k+1))-{\bm{V}}(\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PID}}(k))\;\leq\;-\alpha_{3}(\|\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PID}}(k)\|)+\sigma(\|{\bm{w}}\|)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑽</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ζ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>PID</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝑽</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ζ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>PID</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ζ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>PID</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒘</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{V}}(\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PID}}(k+1))-{\bm{V}}(\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PID}}(k))\;\leq\;-\alpha_{3}(\|\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PID}}(k)\|)+\sigma(\|{\bm{w}}\|).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(62)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_underline">Step 1: Candidtate <math id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{V}}_{PID}(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑽</mi><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{V}}_{PID}(k)</annotation></semantics></math> and PI-closed loop baseline</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Define</p>
<table id="A2.E63" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E63.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{V}}_{\mathrm{PID}}(k)\;:=\;{\bm{V}}_{\mathrm{PI}}\!\big(\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k),k\big)\;+\;r\,\|\Delta\bar{\bm{e}}(k)\|^{2},\qquad r&gt;0," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑽</mi><mi>PID</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">:=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑽</mi><mi>PI</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ζ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>PI</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒆</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{V}}_{\mathrm{PID}}(k)\;:=\;{\bm{V}}_{\mathrm{PI}}\!\big(\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k),k\big)\;+\;r\,\|\Delta\bar{\bm{e}}(k)\|^{2},\qquad r&gt;0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(63)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p6.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{V}}_{\mathrm{PI}}(\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PI}},k)=\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PI}}^{\top}{\bm{P}}(k)\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PI}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑽</mi><mi>PI</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ζ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>PI</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>ζ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>PI</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑷</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ζ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>PI</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{V}}_{\mathrm{PI}}(\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PI}},k)=\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PI}}^{\top}{\bm{P}}(k)\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PI}}</annotation></semantics></math> with
<math id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{P}}(k)={\bm{P}}(k)^{\top}\!\succ 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑷</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝑷</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>≻</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{P}}(k)={\bm{P}}(k)^{\top}\!\succ 0</annotation></semantics></math> and there exists some <math id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\mathrm{PI}}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>PI</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\mathrm{PI}}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that</p>
<table id="A2.E64" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E64.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{M}}_{i}(k)^{\!\top}{\bm{P}}(k)\,{\bm{M}}_{i}(k)\;-\;{\bm{P}}(k)\;\leq\;-\mu_{\mathrm{PI}}I,\qquad\forall k," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑴</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑷</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑴</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">−</mo><mrow><mi>𝑷</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>PI</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{M}}_{i}(k)^{\!\top}{\bm{P}}(k)\,{\bm{M}}_{i}(k)\;-\;{\bm{P}}(k)\;\leq\;-\mu_{\mathrm{PI}}I,\qquad\forall k,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(64)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p6.3" class="ltx_p">Regarding the existence of such <math id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{V}}_{\mathrm{PI}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑽</mi><mi>PI</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{V}}_{\mathrm{PI}}</annotation></semantics></math>, recall the homogeneous PI-loop <math id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k+1)={\bm{M}}_{i}(k)\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ζ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>PI</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑴</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ζ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>PI</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k+1)={\bm{M}}_{i}(k)\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k)</annotation></semantics></math> with
<math id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{M}}_{i}(k)=\begin{bmatrix}{\bm{M}}_{p}(k)&amp;-{\bm{G}}(k)\\
I&amp;I\end{bmatrix}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑴</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>𝑴</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝑮</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>I</mi></mtd><mtd><mi>I</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{M}}_{i}(k)=\begin{bmatrix}{\bm{M}}_{p}(k)&amp;-{\bm{G}}(k)\\
I&amp;I\end{bmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math>,
being asymptotically stable. Suppose there is <math id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{Q}}(k)={\bm{Q}}(k)^{\top}\succeq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑸</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝑸</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>⪰</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{Q}}(k)={\bm{Q}}(k)^{\top}\succeq 0</annotation></semantics></math> bounded so that the pair <math id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="({\bm{M}}_{i}(k),\sqrt{{\bm{Q}}(k)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑴</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>𝑸</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">({\bm{M}}_{i}(k),\sqrt{{\bm{Q}}(k)})</annotation></semantics></math> is observable for all <math id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>, hence the difference Lyapunov equation</p>
<table id="A2.Ex53" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{M}}_{i}^{\top}(k){\bm{P}}(k+1){\bm{M}}_{i}(k)-{\bm{P}}(k)=-{\bm{Q}}(k)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑴</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑷</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑴</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝑷</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝑸</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{M}}_{i}^{\top}(k){\bm{P}}(k+1){\bm{M}}_{i}(k)-{\bm{P}}(k)=-{\bm{Q}}(k)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p6.4" class="ltx_p">admits a unique positive definite solution <math id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{P}}(k)={\bm{P}}^{\top}(k)\succ 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑷</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝑷</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≻</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{P}}(k)={\bm{P}}^{\top}(k)\succ 0</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p6.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>, and a uniform bound <math id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p6.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|{\bm{P}}\|_{\infty}:=\sup_{k}\|{\bm{P}}(k)\|&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝑷</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">:=</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝑷</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|{\bm{P}}\|_{\infty}:=\sup_{k}\|{\bm{P}}(k)\|&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math>
(see <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">(<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gajic &amp; Qureshi, 2008</a>, Ch. 4, p. 110)</cite>)</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_underline">Step 2: Condition (i) as in Eqn. <a href="#A2.E61" title="In B.7.1 Stability of PID closed loop ‣ B.7 PID Control ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Proofs ‣ Activation Steering with a Feedback Controller" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">61</span></a></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p8.1" class="ltx_p">We write <math id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{V}}_{\mathrm{PID}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑽</mi><mi>PID</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{V}}_{\mathrm{PID}}</annotation></semantics></math> as a quadratic form</p>
<table id="A2.E65" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E65.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{V}}_{\mathrm{PID}}(k)\;=\;\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PID}}(k)^{\top}\,{\bm{P}}_{\ast}(k)\,\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PID}}(k),\qquad{\bm{P}}_{\ast}(k)\;:=\;\begin{bmatrix}{\bm{P}}(k)&amp;0\\[2.0pt]
0&amp;rI\end{bmatrix}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑽</mi><mi>PID</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ζ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>PID</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ζ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>PID</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">:=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>𝑷</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{V}}_{\mathrm{PID}}(k)\;=\;\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PID}}(k)^{\top}\,{\bm{P}}_{\ast}(k)\,\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PID}}(k),\qquad{\bm{P}}_{\ast}(k)\;:=\;\begin{bmatrix}{\bm{P}}(k)&amp;0\\[2.0pt]
0&amp;rI\end{bmatrix}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(65)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p8.2" class="ltx_p">Clearly <math id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{P}}_{\ast}(k)={\bm{P}}_{\ast}(k)^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{P}}_{\ast}(k)={\bm{P}}_{\ast}(k)^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{P}}_{\ast}(k)\succ 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≻</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{P}}_{\ast}(k)\succ 0</annotation></semantics></math> because <math id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{P}}(k)\succ 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑷</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≻</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{P}}(k)\succ 0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="rI\succ 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo>≻</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">rI\succ 0</annotation></semantics></math>; hence
<math id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{P}}_{\ast}(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{P}}_{\ast}(k)</annotation></semantics></math> is symmetric positive definite for all <math id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p9.1" class="ltx_p">By the spectral theorem, there exists an orthogonal matrix <math id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{\ast}(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{\ast}(k)</annotation></semantics></math> and a diagonal
<math id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{\ast}(k)=\mathrm{diag}(\lambda_{1}(k),\dots,\lambda_{n_{\ast}}(k))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><msub><mi>n</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{\ast}(k)=\mathrm{diag}(\lambda_{1}(k),\dots,\lambda_{n_{\ast}}(k))</annotation></semantics></math> with positive entries such that
<math id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{P}}_{\ast}(k)=U_{\ast}(k)\Lambda_{\ast}(k)U_{\ast}(k)^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{P}}_{\ast}(k)=U_{\ast}(k)\Lambda_{\ast}(k)U_{\ast}(k)^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Moreover, because <math id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{P}}_{\ast}(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{P}}_{\ast}(k)</annotation></semantics></math> is block diagonal, its eigenvalues are precisely the union of the eigenvalues
of <math id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{P}}(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑷</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{P}}(k)</annotation></semantics></math> and the repeated eigenvalue <math id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>. Using the uniform bounds already established for <math id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{P}}(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑷</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{P}}(k)</annotation></semantics></math>
(there exists <math id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p9.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\lambda}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\lambda}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\min}({\bm{P}}(k))\geq\underline{\lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑷</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\min}({\bm{P}}(k))\geq\underline{\lambda}</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p9.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\max}({\bm{P}}(k))\leq\|{\bm{P}}\|_{\infty}:=\sup_{k}\|{\bm{P}}(k)\|&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑷</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝑷</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">:=</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝑷</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\max}({\bm{P}}(k))\leq\|{\bm{P}}\|_{\infty}:=\sup_{k}\|{\bm{P}}(k)\|&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math>),
we obtain the <math id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p9.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-independent bounds</p>
<table id="A2.Ex54" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex54.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\lambda_{\min}\!\big({\bm{P}}_{\ast}(k)\big)\;\geq\;\underline{\lambda}_{\ast}:=\min\{\underline{\lambda},\,r\}\;&gt;\;0,\qquad\lambda_{\max}\!\big({\bm{P}}_{\ast}(k)\big)\;\leq\;\overline{\lambda}_{\ast}:=\max\{\\
|{\bm{P}}\|_{\infty},\,r\}\;&lt;\;\infty." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≥</mo><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>:=</mo><mi>min</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn> 0</mn><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>:=</mo><mi>max</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝑷</mi><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\min}\!\big({\bm{P}}_{\ast}(k)\big)\;\geq\;\underline{\lambda}_{\ast}:=\min\{\underline{\lambda},\,r\}\;&gt;\;0,\qquad\lambda_{\max}\!\big({\bm{P}}_{\ast}(k)\big)\;\leq\;\overline{\lambda}_{\ast}:=\max\{\\
|{\bm{P}}\|_{\infty},\,r\}\;&lt;\;\infty.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p9.2" class="ltx_p">For every vector <math id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p9.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z</annotation></semantics></math> and every symmetric positive definite <math id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p9.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p9.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\min}(M)\|z\|^{2}\leq z^{\top}Mz\leq\lambda_{\max}(M)\|z\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\min}(M)\|z\|^{2}\leq z^{\top}Mz\leq\lambda_{\max}(M)\|z\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Applying this to <math id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p9.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M={\bm{P}}_{\ast}(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M={\bm{P}}_{\ast}(k)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p9.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z=\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PID}}(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ζ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>PID</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z=\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PID}}(k)</annotation></semantics></math> in Eqn. <a href="#A2.E65" title="In B.7.1 Stability of PID closed loop ‣ B.7 PID Control ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Proofs ‣ Activation Steering with a Feedback Controller" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">65</span></a> yields</p>
<table id="A2.Ex55" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underline{\lambda}_{\ast}\,\big\|\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PID}}(k)\big\|^{2}\;\leq\;{\bm{V}}_{\mathrm{PID}}(k)\;\leq\;\overline{\lambda}_{\ast}\,\big\|\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PID}}(k)\big\|^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ζ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>PID</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑽</mi><mi>PID</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ζ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>PID</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underline{\lambda}_{\ast}\,\big\|\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PID}}(k)\big\|^{2}\;\leq\;{\bm{V}}_{\mathrm{PID}}(k)\;\leq\;\overline{\lambda}_{\ast}\,\big\|\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PID}}(k)\big\|^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p9.3" class="ltx_p">Therefore, choosing the class-<math id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p9.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{K}_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{K}_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math> functions</p>
<table id="A2.Ex56" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{1}({\bm{s}}):=\underline{\lambda}_{\ast}\,{\bm{s}}^{2},\qquad\alpha_{2}({\bm{s}}):=\overline{\lambda}_{\ast}\,{\bm{s}}^{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><munder accentunder="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒔</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒔</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{1}({\bm{s}}):=\underline{\lambda}_{\ast}\,{\bm{s}}^{2},\qquad\alpha_{2}({\bm{s}}):=\overline{\lambda}_{\ast}\,{\bm{s}}^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p9.4" class="ltx_p">we obtain the desired bound</p>
<table id="A2.E66" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E66.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{1}\!\left(\big\|\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PID}}(k)\big\|\right)\;\leq\;{\bm{V}}_{\mathrm{PID}}(k)\;\leq\;\alpha_{2}\!\left(\big\|\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PID}}(k)\big\|\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ζ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>PID</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑽</mi><mi>PID</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ζ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>PID</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{1}\!\left(\big\|\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PID}}(k)\big\|\right)\;\leq\;{\bm{V}}_{\mathrm{PID}}(k)\;\leq\;\alpha_{2}\!\left(\big\|\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PID}}(k)\big\|\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(66)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p9.5" class="ltx_p">which establishes condition (i) in <a href="#A2.E61" title="In B.7.1 Stability of PID closed loop ‣ B.7 PID Control ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Proofs ‣ Activation Steering with a Feedback Controller" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">61</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_underline">Step 3: Condition (ii) as in Eqn. <a href="#A2.E62" title="In B.7.1 Stability of PID closed loop ‣ B.7 PID Control ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Proofs ‣ Activation Steering with a Feedback Controller" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">62</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p11" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p11.1" class="ltx_p">From Eqn. <a href="#A2.E63" title="In B.7.1 Stability of PID closed loop ‣ B.7 PID Control ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Proofs ‣ Activation Steering with a Feedback Controller" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">63</span></a>,</p>
<table id="A2.E67" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E67.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta{\bm{V}}_{\mathrm{PID}}(k)\;=\;\underbrace{\Delta{\bm{V}}_{\mathrm{PI}}\!\left(\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k)\right)\Big|_{\mathrm{PID}}}_{\text{PI part under PID update}}\;+\;r\big(\|\Delta\bar{\bm{e}}(k+1)\|^{2}-\|\Delta\bar{\bm{e}}(k)\|^{2}\big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑽</mi><mi>PID</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><msub><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑽</mi><mi>PI</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ζ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>PI</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mi>PID</mi></msub><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>PI part under PID update</mtext></munder><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒆</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒆</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta{\bm{V}}_{\mathrm{PID}}(k)\;=\;\underbrace{\Delta{\bm{V}}_{\mathrm{PI}}\!\left(\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k)\right)\Big|_{\mathrm{PID}}}_{\text{PI part under PID update}}\;+\;r\big(\|\Delta\bar{\bm{e}}(k+1)\|^{2}-\|\Delta\bar{\bm{e}}(k)\|^{2}\big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(67)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p12" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Bounding the PI part under the PID update.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p13" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p13.1" class="ltx_p">Under PI rule (<math id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{K}}_{d}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑲</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{K}}_{d}=0</annotation></semantics></math>),</p>
<table id="A2.Ex57" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k+1)\big|_{\mathrm{PI}}\;=\;{\bm{M}}_{i}(k)\,\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k)+\tilde{{\bm{w}}}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k),\qquad{\bm{M}}_{i}(k):=\begin{bmatrix}{\bm{M}}_{p}(k)&amp;-{\bm{G}}(k)\\[2.0pt]
I&amp;I\end{bmatrix}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ζ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>PI</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mi>PI</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑴</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ζ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>PI</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒘</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>PI</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑴</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>𝑴</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝑮</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>I</mi></mtd><mtd><mi>I</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k+1)\big|_{\mathrm{PI}}\;=\;{\bm{M}}_{i}(k)\,\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k)+\tilde{{\bm{w}}}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k),\qquad{\bm{M}}_{i}(k):=\begin{bmatrix}{\bm{M}}_{p}(k)&amp;-{\bm{G}}(k)\\[2.0pt]
I&amp;I\end{bmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p13.2" class="ltx_p">then</p>
<table id="A2.EGx21" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex58"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Delta{\bm{V}}_{\mathrm{PI}}\!\left(\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k)\right)\Big|_{\mathrm{PI}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑽</mi><mi>PI</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ζ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>PI</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mi>PI</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Delta{\bm{V}}_{\mathrm{PI}}\!\left(\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k)\right)\Big|_{\mathrm{PI}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex58.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k)^{\!\top}\!\!\big({\bm{M}}_{i}(k)^{\!\top}{\bm{P}}(k{+}1){\bm{M}}_{i}(k)-{\bm{P}}(k)\big)\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ζ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>PI</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑴</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑷</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑴</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝑷</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ζ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>PI</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k)^{\!\top}\!\!\big({\bm{M}}_{i}(k)^{\!\top}{\bm{P}}(k{+}1){\bm{M}}_{i}(k)-{\bm{P}}(k)\big)\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex59"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex59.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad+2\,\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k)^{\!\top}{\bm{M}}_{i}(k)^{\!\top}{\bm{P}}(k{+}1)\,\tilde{\bm{w}}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k)+\tilde{\bm{w}}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k)^{\!\top}{\bm{P}}(k{+}1)\,\tilde{\bm{w}}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ζ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>PI</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑴</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑷</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒘</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>PI</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒘</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>PI</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑷</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒘</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>PI</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad+2\,\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k)^{\!\top}{\bm{M}}_{i}(k)^{\!\top}{\bm{P}}(k{+}1)\,\tilde{\bm{w}}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k)+\tilde{\bm{w}}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k)^{\!\top}{\bm{P}}(k{+}1)\,\tilde{\bm{w}}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p14" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p14.1" class="ltx_p">By Eqn. <a href="#A2.E64" title="In B.7.1 Stability of PID closed loop ‣ B.7 PID Control ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Proofs ‣ Activation Steering with a Feedback Controller" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">64</span></a>, Cauchy-Schwarz inequality and Young’s inequality,</p>
<table id="A2.EGx22" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex61"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex61.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Delta{\bm{V}}_{\mathrm{PI}}\!\left(\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k)\right)\Big|_{\mathrm{PI}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑽</mi><mi>PI</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ζ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>PI</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mi>PI</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Delta{\bm{V}}_{\mathrm{PI}}\!\left(\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k)\right)\Big|_{\mathrm{PI}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex61.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq-\,\mu_{\mathrm{PI}}\,\|\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k)\|^{2}+2\|{\bm{M}}_{i}\|_{\infty}\|{\bm{P}}\|_{\infty}\|\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k)\|\,\|\tilde{\bm{w}}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k)\|+\|{\bm{P}}\|_{\infty}\|\tilde{\bm{w}}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k)\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>PI</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ζ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>PI</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝑴</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝑷</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ζ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>PI</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒘</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>PI</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝑷</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒘</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>PI</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq-\,\mu_{\mathrm{PI}}\,\|\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k)\|^{2}+2\|{\bm{M}}_{i}\|_{\infty}\|{\bm{P}}\|_{\infty}\|\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k)\|\,\|\tilde{\bm{w}}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k)\|+\|{\bm{P}}\|_{\infty}\|\tilde{\bm{w}}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k)\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex62"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex62.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq-(\mu_{\mathrm{PI}}-\varepsilon_{1})\,\|\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k)\|^{2}+\Big(\frac{\|{\bm{M}}_{i}\|_{\infty}^{2}\|{\bm{P}}\|_{\infty}^{2}}{\varepsilon_{1}}+\|{\bm{P}}\|_{\infty}\Big)\|\tilde{\bm{w}}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k)\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>PI</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ζ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>PI</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝑴</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝑷</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝑷</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒘</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>PI</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq-(\mu_{\mathrm{PI}}-\varepsilon_{1})\,\|\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k)\|^{2}+\Big(\frac{\|{\bm{M}}_{i}\|_{\infty}^{2}\|{\bm{P}}\|_{\infty}^{2}}{\varepsilon_{1}}+\|{\bm{P}}\|_{\infty}\Big)\|\tilde{\bm{w}}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k)\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex63"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex63.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\,\mu_{\mathrm{PI}}^{*}\,\|\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k)\|^{2}+C_{1}\|\tilde{\bm{w}}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k)\|^{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>PI</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ζ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>PI</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒘</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>PI</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\,\mu_{\mathrm{PI}}^{*}\,\|\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k)\|^{2}+C_{1}\|\tilde{\bm{w}}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k)\|^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p14.2" class="ltx_p">for any <math id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{1}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{1}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p15" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p15.2" class="ltx_p">Under PID rule (<math id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{K}}_{d}\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑲</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{K}}_{d}\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math>),</p>
<table id="A2.Ex64" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex64.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k+1)\big|_{\mathrm{PID}}\;=\;{\bm{M}}_{i}(k)\,\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k)\;-\;\delta(k)\;+\;{\bm{w}}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ζ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>PI</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mi>PID</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑴</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ζ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>PI</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">−</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>PI</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k+1)\big|_{\mathrm{PID}}\;=\;{\bm{M}}_{i}(k)\,\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k)\;-\;\delta(k)\;+\;{\bm{w}}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p15.3" class="ltx_p">with the “perturbation”</p>
<table id="A2.Ex65" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex65.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta(k):=\begin{bmatrix}H(k)\,\Delta\bar{\bm{e}}(k)\\[2.0pt]
0\end{bmatrix}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒆</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta(k):=\begin{bmatrix}H(k)\,\Delta\bar{\bm{e}}(k)\\[2.0pt]
0\end{bmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p15.4" class="ltx_p">Hence,</p>
<table id="A2.E68" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A2.E68X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E68X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Delta{\bm{V}}_{\mathrm{PI}}\big(\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k)\big)\Big|_{\mathrm{PID}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑽</mi><mi>PI</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ζ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>PI</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mi>PID</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Delta{\bm{V}}_{\mathrm{PI}}\big(\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k)\big)\Big|_{\mathrm{PID}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E68X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle={\bm{V}}_{\mathrm{PI}}\!\big(\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k+1)\big|_{\mathrm{PI}}\big)-{\bm{V}}_{\mathrm{PI}}\!\big(\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k)\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑽</mi><mi>PI</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ζ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>PI</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mi>PI</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑽</mi><mi>PI</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ζ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>PI</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle={\bm{V}}_{\mathrm{PI}}\!\big(\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k+1)\big|_{\mathrm{PI}}\big)-{\bm{V}}_{\mathrm{PI}}\!\big(\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k)\big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(68)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E68Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E68Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle={\bm{V}}_{\mathrm{PI}}\!\big(\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k+1)\big|_{\mathrm{PI}}\big)-{\bm{V}}_{\mathrm{PI}}\!\big(\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k)\big)+2\big(\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k+1)\big|_{\mathrm{PI}}\big)^{\!\top}{\bm{P}}\,\delta(k)+\delta(k)^{\!\top}{\bm{P}}\,\delta(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑽</mi><mi>PI</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ζ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>PI</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mi>PI</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑽</mi><mi>PI</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ζ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>PI</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ζ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>PI</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mi>PI</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑷</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑷</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle={\bm{V}}_{\mathrm{PI}}\!\big(\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k+1)\big|_{\mathrm{PI}}\big)-{\bm{V}}_{\mathrm{PI}}\!\big(\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k)\big)+2\big(\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k+1)\big|_{\mathrm{PI}}\big)^{\!\top}{\bm{P}}\,\delta(k)+\delta(k)^{\!\top}{\bm{P}}\,\delta(k)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p16" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p16.1" class="ltx_p">Bounding each term in Eqn. <a href="#A2.E68" title="In B.7.1 Stability of PID closed loop ‣ B.7 PID Control ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Proofs ‣ Activation Steering with a Feedback Controller" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">68</span></a></p>
<ul id="A2.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A2.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{V}}_{\mathrm{PI}}\!\big(\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k+1)\big|_{\mathrm{PI}}\big)-{\bm{V}}_{\mathrm{PI}}\!\big(\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k)\big)\leq-\mu_{\mathrm{PI}}^{*}\|\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k)\|^{2}+C_{1}\|\tilde{\bm{w}}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k)\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑽</mi><mi>PI</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ζ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>PI</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mi>PI</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑽</mi><mi>PI</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ζ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>PI</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>PI</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ζ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>PI</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒘</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>PI</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{V}}_{\mathrm{PI}}\!\big(\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k+1)\big|_{\mathrm{PI}}\big)-{\bm{V}}_{\mathrm{PI}}\!\big(\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k)\big)\leq-\mu_{\mathrm{PI}}^{*}\|\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k)\|^{2}+C_{1}\|\tilde{\bm{w}}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k)\|</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Applying Young’s inequality for inner product, there exists <math id="A2.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> s.t</p>
<table id="A2.EGx23" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E69"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E69.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 2\big(\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k+1)\big|_{\mathrm{PI}}\big)^{\!\top}{\bm{P}}\delta(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ζ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>PI</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mi>PI</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑷</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 2\big(\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k+1)\big|_{\mathrm{PI}}\big)^{\!\top}{\bm{P}}\delta(k)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E69.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\varepsilon\big\|\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k+1)\big|_{\mathrm{PI}}\big\|^{2}+\tfrac{1}{\varepsilon}\delta(k)^{\!\top}{\bm{P}}\delta(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><msub><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ζ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>PI</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mi>PI</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>ε</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑷</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\varepsilon\big\|\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k+1)\big|_{\mathrm{PI}}\big\|^{2}+\tfrac{1}{\varepsilon}\delta(k)^{\!\top}{\bm{P}}\delta(k)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(69)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E70"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E70.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\varepsilon\|{\bm{P}}\|\big\|\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k+1)\big|_{\mathrm{PI}}\big\|^{2}+\tfrac{\|{\bm{P}}\|}{\varepsilon}M^{2}\ell^{2}\|\Delta\bar{\bm{e}}(k)\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝑷</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><msub><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ζ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>PI</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mi>PI</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝑷</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>ε</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒆</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\varepsilon\|{\bm{P}}\|\big\|\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k+1)\big|_{\mathrm{PI}}\big\|^{2}+\tfrac{\|{\bm{P}}\|}{\varepsilon}M^{2}\ell^{2}\|\Delta\bar{\bm{e}}(k)\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(70)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.I2.i2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I2.i2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A2.I2.i2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\big\|\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k+1)\big|_{\mathrm{PI}}\big\|^{2}\leq 2\|{\bm{M}}_{i}\|_{\infty}^{2}\|\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k)\|^{2}+2\|\tilde{\bm{w}}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k)\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><msub><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ζ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>PI</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mi>PI</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝑴</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ζ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>PI</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒘</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>PI</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\big\|\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k+1)\big|_{\mathrm{PI}}\big\|^{2}\leq 2\|{\bm{M}}_{i}\|_{\infty}^{2}\|\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k)\|^{2}+2\|\tilde{\bm{w}}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k)\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
<table id="A2.EGx24" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex66"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex66.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Rightarrow 2\big(\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k+1)\big|_{\mathrm{PI}}\big)^{\!\top}{\bm{P}}\delta(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">⇒</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ζ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>PI</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mi>PI</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑷</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Rightarrow 2\big(\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k+1)\big|_{\mathrm{PI}}\big)^{\!\top}{\bm{P}}\delta(k)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex66.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq 2\varepsilon\|{\bm{P}}\|\|{\bm{M}}_{i}\|_{\infty}^{2}\|\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k)\|^{2}+2\varepsilon\|{\bm{P}}\|\|\tilde{\bm{w}}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k)\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝑷</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝑴</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ζ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>PI</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝑷</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒘</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>PI</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq 2\varepsilon\|{\bm{P}}\|\|{\bm{M}}_{i}\|_{\infty}^{2}\|\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k)\|^{2}+2\varepsilon\|{\bm{P}}\|\|\tilde{\bm{w}}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k)\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
