<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.I2.i2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.I2.i2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{2}=2\varepsilon\|{\bm{P}}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝑷</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{2}=2\varepsilon\|{\bm{P}}\|</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.I2.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta(k)^{\!\top}{\bm{P}}\delta(k)\leq\|{\bm{P}}\|\|\delta(k)\|^{2}\leq\|{\bm{P}}\|M^{2}\ell^{2}\|\Delta\bar{\bm{e}}(k)\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑷</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝑷</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝑷</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒆</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta(k)^{\!\top}{\bm{P}}\delta(k)\leq\|{\bm{P}}\|\|\delta(k)\|^{2}\leq\|{\bm{P}}\|M^{2}\ell^{2}\|\Delta\bar{\bm{e}}(k)\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p17" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p17.2" class="ltx_p">Therefore,</p>
<table id="A2.E71" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A2.E71X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E71X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Delta{\bm{V}}_{\mathrm{PI}}\!\big(\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k)\big)\Big|_{\mathrm{PID}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑽</mi><mi>PI</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ζ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>PI</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mi>PID</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Delta{\bm{V}}_{\mathrm{PI}}\!\big(\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k)\big)\Big|_{\mathrm{PID}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E71X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq-\mu_{\mathrm{PI}}^{*}\|\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k)\|^{2}+C_{1}\|\tilde{\bm{w}}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k)\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>PI</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ζ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>PI</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒘</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>PI</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq-\mu_{\mathrm{PI}}^{*}\|\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k)\|^{2}+C_{1}\|\tilde{\bm{w}}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k)\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="5" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(71)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E71Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E71Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+2\varepsilon\|{\bm{P}}\|\|{\bm{M}}_{i}\|_{\infty}^{2}\|\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k)\|^{2}+\tfrac{\|{\bm{P}}\|}{\varepsilon}M^{2}\ell^{2}\|\Delta\bar{\bm{e}}(k)\|^{2}+C_{2}\|\tilde{\bm{w}}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k)\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝑷</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝑴</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ζ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>PI</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝑷</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>ε</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒆</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒘</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>PI</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+2\varepsilon\|{\bm{P}}\|\|{\bm{M}}_{i}\|_{\infty}^{2}\|\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k)\|^{2}+\tfrac{\|{\bm{P}}\|}{\varepsilon}M^{2}\ell^{2}\|\Delta\bar{\bm{e}}(k)\|^{2}+C_{2}\|\tilde{\bm{w}}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k)\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E71Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E71Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\|{\bm{P}}\|M^{2}\ell^{2}\|\Delta\bar{\bm{e}}(k)\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝑷</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒆</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\|{\bm{P}}\|M^{2}\ell^{2}\|\Delta\bar{\bm{e}}(k)\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E71Xc" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E71Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-(\mu_{\mathrm{PI}}^{*}-2\varepsilon\|{\bm{P}}\|\|{\bm{M}}_{i}\|_{\infty}^{2})\|\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k)\|^{2}+\|{\bm{P}}\|M^{2}\ell^{2}\Big(\tfrac{1}{\varepsilon}+1\Big)\|\Delta\bar{\bm{e}}(k)\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>PI</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝑷</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝑴</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ζ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>PI</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝑷</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>ε</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒆</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-(\mu_{\mathrm{PI}}^{*}-2\varepsilon\|{\bm{P}}\|\|{\bm{M}}_{i}\|_{\infty}^{2})\|\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k)\|^{2}+\|{\bm{P}}\|M^{2}\ell^{2}\Big(\tfrac{1}{\varepsilon}+1\Big)\|\Delta\bar{\bm{e}}(k)\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E71Xd" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E71Xd.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+C_{3}\|\tilde{\bm{w}}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k)\|^{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒘</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>PI</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+C_{3}\|\tilde{\bm{w}}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k)\|^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p17.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{3}=C_{1}+C_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{3}=C_{1}+C_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p18" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p18.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p18.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Bounding the increment term.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p19" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p19.2" class="ltx_p">From Eqn. <a href="#A2.E59" title="In B.7.1 Stability of PID closed loop ‣ B.7 PID Control ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Proofs ‣ Activation Steering with a Feedback Controller" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">59</span></a> and applying the inequality <math id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x+y+z)^{2}\leq 3(x^{2}+y^{2}+z^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x+y+z)^{2}\leq 3(x^{2}+y^{2}+z^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A2.Ex70" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex70.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\Delta\bar{\bm{e}}(k+1)\|^{2}\;\leq\;3\Big(\|{\bm{M}}_{p}(k)-I\|_{\infty}^{2}+Mh\Big)\,\|\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k)\|^{2}\;+\;3M^{2}\ell^{2}\,\|\Delta\bar{\bm{e}}(k)\|^{2}\;+\;3\|\tilde{\bm{w}}_{\mathrm{PID}}(k)\|^{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒆</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn> 3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑴</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ζ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>PI</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn> 3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒆</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn> 3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒘</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>PID</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\Delta\bar{\bm{e}}(k+1)\|^{2}\;\leq\;3\Big(\|{\bm{M}}_{p}(k)-I\|_{\infty}^{2}+Mh\Big)\,\|\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k)\|^{2}\;+\;3M^{2}\ell^{2}\,\|\Delta\bar{\bm{e}}(k)\|^{2}\;+\;3\|\tilde{\bm{w}}_{\mathrm{PID}}(k)\|^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p19.3" class="ltx_p">and so</p>
<table id="A2.E72" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A2.E72X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E72X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle r\big(\|\Delta\bar{\bm{e}}(k+1)\|^{2}-\|\Delta\bar{\bm{e}}(k)\|^{2}\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒆</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒆</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle r\big(\|\Delta\bar{\bm{e}}(k+1)\|^{2}-\|\Delta\bar{\bm{e}}(k)\|^{2}\big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E72X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\;3r\Big(\|{\bm{M}}_{p}(k)-I\|_{\infty}^{2}+Mh\Big)\,\|\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k)\|^{2}\;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn> 3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑴</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ζ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>PI</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\;3r\Big(\|{\bm{M}}_{p}(k)-I\|_{\infty}^{2}+Mh\Big)\,\|\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k)\|^{2}\;</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(72)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E72Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E72Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\;r\big(1-3M^{2}\ell^{2}\big)\|\Delta\bar{\bm{e}}(k)\|^{2}\;+\;3r\|\tilde{\bm{w}}_{\mathrm{PID}}(k)\|^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒆</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn> 3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒘</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>PID</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\;r\big(1-3M^{2}\ell^{2}\big)\|\Delta\bar{\bm{e}}(k)\|^{2}\;+\;3r\|\tilde{\bm{w}}_{\mathrm{PID}}(k)\|^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p20" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p20.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p20.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Combination</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p21" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p21.1" class="ltx_p">Combining Eqn. <a href="#A2.E67" title="In B.7.1 Stability of PID closed loop ‣ B.7 PID Control ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Proofs ‣ Activation Steering with a Feedback Controller" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">67</span></a>, Ineq. <a href="#A2.E71" title="In B.7.1 Stability of PID closed loop ‣ B.7 PID Control ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Proofs ‣ Activation Steering with a Feedback Controller" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">71</span></a>, and Ineq. <a href="#A2.E72" title="In B.7.1 Stability of PID closed loop ‣ B.7 PID Control ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Proofs ‣ Activation Steering with a Feedback Controller" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">72</span></a>,</p>
<table id="A2.EGx25" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex71"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex71.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Delta{\bm{V}}_{\mathrm{PID}}(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑽</mi><mi>PID</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Delta{\bm{V}}_{\mathrm{PID}}(k)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex71.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq-\Big(\mu_{\mathrm{PI}}^{*}-2\varepsilon\|{\bm{P}}\|_{\infty}\,\|{\bm{M}}_{i}\|_{\infty}^{2}-3r\big(\|{\bm{M}}_{p}(k)-I\|_{\infty}^{2}+Mh\big)\Big)\,\|\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k)\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>PI</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝑷</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝑴</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑴</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ζ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>PI</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq-\Big(\mu_{\mathrm{PI}}^{*}-2\varepsilon\|{\bm{P}}\|_{\infty}\,\|{\bm{M}}_{i}\|_{\infty}^{2}-3r\big(\|{\bm{M}}_{p}(k)-I\|_{\infty}^{2}+Mh\big)\Big)\,\|\tilde{\zeta}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k)\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex72"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex72.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad-\Big(r(1-3M^{2}\ell^{2})-\|{\bm{P}}\|_{\infty}M^{2}\ell^{2}\Big(\tfrac{1}{\varepsilon}+1\Big)\Big)\,\|\Delta\bar{\bm{e}}(k)\|^{2}\;+\;C\,\|\tilde{\bm{w}}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k)\|^{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝑷</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>ε</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒆</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒘</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>PI</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad-\Big(r(1-3M^{2}\ell^{2})-\|{\bm{P}}\|_{\infty}M^{2}\ell^{2}\Big(\tfrac{1}{\varepsilon}+1\Big)\Big)\,\|\Delta\bar{\bm{e}}(k)\|^{2}\;+\;C\,\|\tilde{\bm{w}}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k)\|^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p21.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C=C_{3}+r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C=C_{3}+r</annotation></semantics></math>. Define</p>
<table id="A2.EGx26" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E73"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E73.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle S(r,\varepsilon):=\mu_{\mathrm{PI}}^{*}-2\varepsilon\|{\bm{P}}\|_{\infty}\,\|{\bm{M}}_{i}\|_{\infty}^{2}-3r\big(\|{\bm{M}}_{p}(k)-I\|_{\infty}^{2}+Mh\big),\quad" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>PI</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝑷</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝑴</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑴</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle S(r,\varepsilon):=\mu_{\mathrm{PI}}^{*}-2\varepsilon\|{\bm{P}}\|_{\infty}\,\|{\bm{M}}_{i}\|_{\infty}^{2}-3r\big(\|{\bm{M}}_{p}(k)-I\|_{\infty}^{2}+Mh\big),\quad</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(73)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E74"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E74.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle T(r,\varepsilon,\ell):=r(1-3M^{2}\ell^{2})-\|{\bm{P}}\|_{\infty}M^{2}\ell^{2}\Big(\tfrac{1}{\varepsilon}+1\Big)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝑷</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>ε</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle T(r,\varepsilon,\ell):=r(1-3M^{2}\ell^{2})-\|{\bm{P}}\|_{\infty}M^{2}\ell^{2}\Big(\tfrac{1}{\varepsilon}+1\Big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(74)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p22" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p22.1" class="ltx_p">ISS of the PID loop follows if <math id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S(r,\varepsilon)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S(r,\varepsilon)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p22.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T(r,\varepsilon,\ell)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T(r,\varepsilon,\ell)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p23" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p23.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p23.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Feasible choices.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p24" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p24.1" class="ltx_p">We are free to choose any <math id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p24.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p24.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S(r,\varepsilon)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S(r,\varepsilon)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.
One convenient selection is</p>
<table id="A2.Ex73" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex73.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\varepsilon=\frac{\mu_{\mathrm{PI}}^{*}}{8\,\|{\bm{P}}\|_{\infty}\,\|{\bm{M}}_{i}\|_{\infty}^{2}},\qquad r=\frac{\mu_{\mathrm{PI}}^{*}}{8\big(\|{\bm{M}}_{p}(k)-I\|_{\infty}^{2}+Mh\big)}\quad\Rightarrow\quad S(r,\varepsilon)=\tfrac{3}{8}\mu_{\mathrm{PI}}^{*}&gt;0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>PI</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝑷</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝑴</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>PI</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑴</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">⇒</mo><mi>S</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac></mstyle><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>PI</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon=\frac{\mu_{\mathrm{PI}}^{*}}{8\,\|{\bm{P}}\|_{\infty}\,\|{\bm{M}}_{i}\|_{\infty}^{2}},\qquad r=\frac{\mu_{\mathrm{PI}}^{*}}{8\big(\|{\bm{M}}_{p}(k)-I\|_{\infty}^{2}+Mh\big)}\quad\Rightarrow\quad S(r,\varepsilon)=\tfrac{3}{8}\mu_{\mathrm{PI}}^{*}&gt;0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p24.2" class="ltx_p">With <math id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p24.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon,r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon,r</annotation></semantics></math> fixed as above, pick <math id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p24.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> small enough to satisfy <math id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p24.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T(r,\varepsilon,\ell)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T(r,\varepsilon,\ell)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, namely</p>
<table id="A2.Ex74" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex74.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell^{2}\;&lt;\;\frac{r}{\big(\,\|{\bm{P}}\|_{\infty}\big(\tfrac{1}{\varepsilon}+1\big)+3r\,\big)M^{2}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">&lt;</mo><mfrac><mi>r</mi><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.170em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝑷</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>ε</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell^{2}\;&lt;\;\frac{r}{\big(\,\|{\bm{P}}\|_{\infty}\big(\tfrac{1}{\varepsilon}+1\big)+3r\,\big)M^{2}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p24.3" class="ltx_p">Under these choices, <math id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p24.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta{\bm{V}}_{\mathrm{PID}}(k)\leq-\alpha_{3}\|\zeta_{\mathrm{PI}}(k)\|^{2}-\alpha_{4}\|\Delta\bar{\bm{e}}(k)\|^{2}+\beta\,\|{\bm{w}}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k)\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑽</mi><mi>PID</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mi>PI</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒆</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>PI</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta{\bm{V}}_{\mathrm{PID}}(k)\leq-\alpha_{3}\|\zeta_{\mathrm{PI}}(k)\|^{2}-\alpha_{4}\|\Delta\bar{\bm{e}}(k)\|^{2}+\beta\,\|{\bm{w}}_{\mathrm{PI}}(k)\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p24.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{3},\alpha_{4},\beta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{3},\alpha_{4},\beta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, which satisfies condition (ii) as in Eqn. <a href="#A2.E62" title="In B.7.1 Stability of PID closed loop ‣ B.7 PID Control ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Proofs ‣ Activation Steering with a Feedback Controller" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">62</span></a> and proves ISS of the PID closed loop.  <math id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p24.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\square" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\square</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS7.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">B.7.2 </span>Overshooting under PID law of control</h4>

<div id="A2.SS7.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Developing from Sec. <a href="#A2.SS6" title="B.6 Oveshoot Mechanism ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Proofs ‣ Activation Steering with a Feedback Controller" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.6</span></a>, we introduce scalar PID recursion along <math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A2.E75" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E75.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{e}}_{v}(k+1)=a(k)\,{\bm{e}}_{v}(k)-b(k)\,{\bm{s}}_{v}(k)-c(k)\,\Delta{\bm{e}}_{v}(k)+{\bm{w}}_{v}^{\perp}(k),\qquad{\bm{s}}_{v}(k+1)={\bm{s}}_{v}(k)+{\bm{e}}_{v}(k)-d_{v}(k)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>v</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{e}}_{v}(k+1)=a(k)\,{\bm{e}}_{v}(k)-b(k)\,{\bm{s}}_{v}(k)-c(k)\,\Delta{\bm{e}}_{v}(k)+{\bm{w}}_{v}^{\perp}(k),\qquad{\bm{s}}_{v}(k+1)={\bm{s}}_{v}(k)+{\bm{e}}_{v}(k)-d_{v}(k),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(75)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where</p>
<table id="A2.Ex75" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex75.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a(k):=v^{\top}{\bm{M}}_{p}(k)v,\qquad b(k):=v^{\top}{\bm{G}}(k)v,\qquad c(k):=v^{\top}{\bm{H}}(k)v," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑴</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑮</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑯</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a(k):=v^{\top}{\bm{M}}_{p}(k)v,\qquad b(k):=v^{\top}{\bm{G}}(k)v,\qquad c(k):=v^{\top}{\bm{H}}(k)v,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A2.Ex76" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex76.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta{\bm{e}}_{v}(k)=v^{\top}\Delta\bar{{\bm{e}}}(k),\quad{\bm{w}}_{v}^{\perp}(k)=v^{\top}{\bm{w}}^{\perp}(k)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒆</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>v</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒘</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta{\bm{e}}_{v}(k)=v^{\top}\Delta\bar{{\bm{e}}}(k),\quad{\bm{w}}_{v}^{\perp}(k)=v^{\top}{\bm{w}}^{\perp}(k).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">By construction <math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a(k)\leq q&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a(k)\leq q&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b(k)\leq Mh" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b(k)\leq Mh</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c(k)\leq M\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c(k)\leq M\ell</annotation></semantics></math> with
<math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M:=\sup_{k}\|\bar{\bm{A}}(k)\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo rspace="0.1389em">:=</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M:=\sup_{k}\|\bar{\bm{A}}(k)\|</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h:=\|{\bm{K}}_{i}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝑲</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h:=\|{\bm{K}}_{i}\|</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell:=\|{\bm{K}}_{d}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝑲</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell:=\|{\bm{K}}_{d}\|</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We now impose an additional requirement on the derivative gain <math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{K}}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑲</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{K}}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>
so that, without the effect of noise, the PID update secures the
monotonic decrease of <math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{e}}_{v}(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{e}}_{v}(k)</annotation></semantics></math> before the first negative peak of scalar error <math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{e}}_{v}(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{e}}_{v}(k)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmremark4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmremark4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark 4</span></span><span id="Thmremark4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> (Pre-overshoot monotonic decrease of scalar errors)</span></h6>
<div id="Thmremark4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmremark4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmremark4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Assume the setting of Proposition <a href="#Thmproposition4" title="Proposition 4 (Agressive PI gain leads to a large first overshoot) ‣ Scalarization along a direction. ‣ B.6 Oveshoot Mechanism ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Proofs ‣ Activation Steering with a Feedback Controller" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> and further suppose the scalar error trajectory before the first largest overshoot under PID law is <em id="Thmremark4.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">smooth</em> in the sense that there exists <math id="Thmremark4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<table id="A2.E76" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E76.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{{\bm{e}}_{v}(k-1)}{{\bm{e}}_{v}(k)}\;\leq\;R\qquad\text{for all }\penalty\ k=1,2,\dots,i_{max}-1," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">for all </mtext><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{{\bm{e}}_{v}(k-1)}{{\bm{e}}_{v}(k)}\;\leq\;R\qquad\text{for all }\penalty\ k=1,2,\dots,i_{max}-1,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(76)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmremark4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmremark4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmremark4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{A}}_{0}\ :=\ \max_{k_{0}\leq i\leq k_{1}}\,|{\bm{e}}_{v}(i)|\ =|{\bm{e}}_{v}(i_{max})|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐀</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="0.778em">:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{A}}_{0}\ :=\ \max_{k_{0}\leq i\leq k_{1}}\,|{\bm{e}}_{v}(i)|\ =|{\bm{e}}_{v}(i_{max})|</annotation></semantics></math> from Eqn.<a href="#A2.E53" title="In Proposition 4 (Agressive PI gain leads to a large first overshoot) ‣ Scalarization along a direction. ‣ B.6 Oveshoot Mechanism ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Proofs ‣ Activation Steering with a Feedback Controller" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">53</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Thmremark4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmremark4.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmremark4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Assume that <math id="Thmremark4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{w}}_{v}^{\perp}\!\equiv 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐰</mi><mi>v</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.108em">≡</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{w}}_{v}^{\perp}\!\equiv 0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmremark4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{d}}_{v}\!\equiv 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐝</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.108em">≡</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{d}}_{v}\!\equiv 0</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Thmremark4.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmremark4.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmremark4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If, in addition, the derivative gain satisfies</span></p>
<table id="A2.E77" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E77.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l=\|{\bm{K}}_{d}\|\ \leq\ \frac{1-q}{(R-1)M}\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝑲</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l=\|{\bm{K}}_{d}\|\ \leq\ \frac{1-q}{(R-1)M}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(77)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmremark4.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmremark4.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">then under PID law</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex77" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex77.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{e}}_{v}(k+1)\ \leq\ {\bm{e}}_{v}(k)\qquad\text{for all }\penalty\ k=0,1,\dots,i_{max}-1." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">for all </mtext><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{e}}_{v}(k+1)\ \leq\ {\bm{e}}_{v}(k)\qquad\text{for all }\penalty\ k=0,1,\dots,i_{max}-1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS7.SSS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof.</span>
Before <math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{e}}_{v}(k)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{e}}_{v}(k)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{s}}_{v}(k)\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{s}}_{v}(k)\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> (since <math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{s}}_{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{s}}_{v}</annotation></semantics></math> accumulates <math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{e}}_{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{e}}_{v}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{s}}_{v}(0)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{s}}_{v}(0)=0</annotation></semantics></math>).
For <math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{0}\leq k\leq i_{max}-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{0}\leq k\leq i_{max}-1</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{s}}_{v}(k)\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{s}}_{v}(k)\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> proved in remark <a href="#Thmremark5" title="Remark 5 (before the first negative peak, the integral state is positive) ‣ B.7.2 Overshooting under PID law of control ‣ B.7 PID Control ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Proofs ‣ Activation Steering with a Feedback Controller" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Hence</p>
<table id="A2.Ex78" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex78X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex78X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\bm{e}}_{v}(k+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\bm{e}}_{v}(k+1)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex78X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=a(k){\bm{e}}_{v}(k)-b(k){\bm{s}}_{v}(k)-c(k)\big({\bm{e}}_{v}(k)-{\bm{e}}_{v}(k-1)\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=a(k){\bm{e}}_{v}(k)-b(k){\bm{s}}_{v}(k)-c(k)\big({\bm{e}}_{v}(k)-{\bm{e}}_{v}(k-1)\big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex78Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex78Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq a(k){\bm{e}}_{v}(k)+c(k)\big({\bm{e}}_{v}(k-1)-{\bm{e}}_{v}(k)\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq a(k){\bm{e}}_{v}(k)+c(k)\big({\bm{e}}_{v}(k-1)-{\bm{e}}_{v}(k)\big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex78Xb"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex78Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\Big[a(k)+c(k)\,(R-1)\Big]{\bm{e}}_{v}(k)\ \leq\ \Big[q+(R-1)M\ell\Big]{\bm{e}}_{v}(k)\ \leq\ {\bm{e}}_{v}(k)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\Big[a(k)+c(k)\,(R-1)\Big]{\bm{e}}_{v}(k)\ \leq\ \Big[q+(R-1)M\ell\Big]{\bm{e}}_{v}(k)\ \leq\ {\bm{e}}_{v}(k),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS2.p4.2" class="ltx_p">where the last inequality is exactly Eqn. <a href="#A2.E77" title="In Remark 4 (Pre-overshoot monotonic decrease of scalar errors) ‣ B.7.2 Overshooting under PID law of control ‣ B.7 PID Control ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Proofs ‣ Activation Steering with a Feedback Controller" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">77</span></a>.
 <math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\square" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\square</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS7.SSS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Note for <math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>:</span> In practice, one may estimate a conservative <math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> from PI-law traces
and use a small safety factor</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS2.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A2.SS7.SSS2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Adding Disturbance:</em>
With bounded disturbances, the scalar update reads</p>
<table id="A2.Ex79" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex79.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{e}}_{v}(k+1)\ \leq\ \big[q+(R-1)c_{\max}\big]\,{\bm{e}}_{v}(k)\ +\ |{\bm{w}}_{v}^{\perp}(k)|\ ," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.722em">+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>v</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{e}}_{v}(k+1)\ \leq\ \big[q+(R-1)c_{\max}\big]\,{\bm{e}}_{v}(k)\ +\ |{\bm{w}}_{v}^{\perp}(k)|\ ,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS2.p6.2" class="ltx_p">so the same one-step monotonicity conclusion holds whenever</p>
<table id="A2.Ex80" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex80.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|{\bm{w}}_{v}^{\perp}(k)|\leq\ \Big(1-\big[q+(R-1)c_{\max}\big]\Big)\,{\bm{e}}_{v}(k)\quad\text{for all pre-first-largest-overshooting steps}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>v</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>for all pre-first-largest-overshooting steps</mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|{\bm{w}}_{v}^{\perp}(k)|\leq\ \Big(1-\big[q+(R-1)c_{\max}\big]\Big)\,{\bm{e}}_{v}(k)\quad\text{for all pre-first-largest-overshooting steps}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS2.p6.3" class="ltx_p">If this smallness condition on disturbances fails at some step, one-step monotonicity may be lost, but the ISS bounds proved earlier still guarantee geometric decay up to a disturbance-dependent radius.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmremark5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmremark5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark 5</span></span><span id="Thmremark5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> (before the first negative peak, the integral state is positive)</span></h6>
<div id="Thmremark5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmremark5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmremark5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Assume the setting of Remark. <a href="#Thmremark4" title="Remark 4 (Pre-overshoot monotonic decrease of scalar errors) ‣ B.7.2 Overshooting under PID law of control ‣ B.7 PID Control ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Proofs ‣ Activation Steering with a Feedback Controller" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>. Hence,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex81" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex81.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{s}}_{v}(k)\;&gt;\;0\qquad\text{for all }k=k_{0},\dots,i_{\max}-1." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn> 0</mn></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">for all </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{s}}_{v}(k)\;&gt;\;0\qquad\text{for all }k=k_{0},\dots,i_{\max}-1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS2.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS7.SSS2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof.</span>
We argue by contradiction. Suppose there exists the first <math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau\in[k_{0},i_{\max}-1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau\in[k_{0},i_{\max}-1]</annotation></semantics></math> such that
<math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{s}}_{v}(\tau)\leq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{s}}_{v}(\tau)\leq 0</annotation></semantics></math>. Then <math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{s}}_{v}(\tau-1)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{s}}_{v}(\tau-1)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, and since we are on the first negative lobe,
<math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{e}}_{v}(\tau)&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{e}}_{v}(\tau)&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. Compute the one-step change of <math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{e}}_{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{e}}_{v}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex82" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex82X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex82X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\bm{e}}_{v}(\tau{+}1)-{\bm{e}}_{v}(\tau)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\bm{e}}_{v}(\tau{+}1)-{\bm{e}}_{v}(\tau)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex82X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(a(\tau)-1){\bm{e}}_{v}(\tau)-b(\tau){\bm{s}}_{v}(\tau)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(a(\tau)-1){\bm{e}}_{v}(\tau)-b(\tau){\bm{s}}_{v}(\tau)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex82Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex82Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(1-a(\tau))\,|{\bm{e}}_{v}(\tau)|\;+\;b(\tau)\,(-{\bm{s}}_{v}(\tau))\;\;&gt;\;0," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.560em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn> 0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(1-a(\tau))\,|{\bm{e}}_{v}(\tau)|\;+\;b(\tau)\,(-{\bm{s}}_{v}(\tau))\;\;&gt;\;0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS2.p7.2" class="ltx_p">because <math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a(\tau)\leq q&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a(\tau)\leq q&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{e}}_{v}(\tau)&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{e}}_{v}(\tau)&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{s}}_{v}(\tau)\leq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{s}}_{v}(\tau)\leq 0</annotation></semantics></math>.
Hence <math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.p7.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{e}}_{v}(\tau{+}1)&gt;{\bm{e}}_{v}(\tau)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{e}}_{v}(\tau{+}1)&gt;{\bm{e}}_{v}(\tau)</annotation></semantics></math>.
By the same reasoning, as long as both <math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.p7.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{e}}_{v}(k)&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{e}}_{v}(k)&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.p7.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{s}}_{v}(k)\leq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{s}}_{v}(k)\leq 0</annotation></semantics></math> hold, we have</p>
<table id="A2.Ex83" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex83.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{e}}_{v}(k{+}1)-{\bm{e}}_{v}(k)\geq(1-q)\,|{\bm{e}}_{v}(k)|+b_{\min}\,(-{\bm{s}}_{v}(k))&gt;0," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{e}}_{v}(k{+}1)-{\bm{e}}_{v}(k)\geq(1-q)\,|{\bm{e}}_{v}(k)|+b_{\min}\,(-{\bm{s}}_{v}(k))&gt;0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS2.p7.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.p7.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{\min}:=\inf_{k}b(k)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">:=</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.167em">inf</mo><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{\min}:=\inf_{k}b(k)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.
Meanwhile <math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.p7.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{s}}_{v}(k{+}1)={\bm{s}}_{v}(k)+{\bm{e}}_{v}(k)\leq{\bm{s}}_{v}(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{s}}_{v}(k{+}1)={\bm{s}}_{v}(k)+{\bm{e}}_{v}(k)\leq{\bm{s}}_{v}(k)</annotation></semantics></math> on that interval, so <math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.p7.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{s}}_{v}(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{s}}_{v}(k)</annotation></semantics></math> is non-increasing; equivalenty <math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.p7.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-{\bm{s}}_{v}(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-{\bm{s}}_{v}(k)</annotation></semantics></math> is non-decreasing.
If <math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.p7.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{e}}_{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{e}}_{v}</annotation></semantics></math> stayed negative forever, then
<math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.p7.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k=0}^{N}{\bm{e}}_{v}(\tau{+}k)\to-\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k=0}^{N}{\bm{e}}_{v}(\tau{+}k)\to-\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.p7.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-{\bm{s}}_{v}(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-{\bm{s}}_{v}(k)</annotation></semantics></math> would grow without bound and the
increments <math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.p7.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{e}}_{v}(k{+}1)-{\bm{e}}_{v}(k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{e}}_{v}(k{+}1)-{\bm{e}}_{v}(k)</annotation></semantics></math> would eventually be arbitrarily large, forcing <math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.p7.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{e}}_{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{e}}_{v}</annotation></semantics></math> to
cross <math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.p7.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> in finite time. This contradicts the choice of <math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.p7.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math> as the first
negative peak. Therefore such <math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.p7.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> cannot exist and <math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.p7.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{s}}_{v}(k)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{s}}_{v}(k)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> for all
<math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.p7.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=k_{0},\dots,i_{\max}-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=k_{0},\dots,i_{\max}-1</annotation></semantics></math>.  <math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.p7.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\square" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\square</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS2.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS2.p8.1" class="ltx_p">See <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2 (PID reduces the first-overshoot amplitude) ‣ 4.2.2 PID Control ‣ 4.2 Stability of the Error Dynamics: Roles and Caveats of PI and PID Control ‣ 4 Theoretical Analysis of PID Steering ‣ Activation Steering with a Feedback Controller" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>
<span id="A2.SS7.SSS2.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof.</span>
Under the PI law we have</p>
<table id="A2.Ex84" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex84.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{0}^{\mathrm{PI}}=-a(i_{max}\!-\!1)\,{\bm{e}}_{v}(i_{max}\!-\!1)+b(i_{max}\!-\!1)\,{\bm{s}}_{v}(i_{max}\!-\!1)-{\bm{w}}_{v}^{\perp}(i_{max}\!-\!1)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>PI</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>v</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{0}^{\mathrm{PI}}=-a(i_{max}\!-\!1)\,{\bm{e}}_{v}(i_{max}\!-\!1)+b(i_{max}\!-\!1)\,{\bm{s}}_{v}(i_{max}\!-\!1)-{\bm{w}}_{v}^{\perp}(i_{max}\!-\!1),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS2.p8.2" class="ltx_p">while under the PID law</p>
<table id="A2.EGx27" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E78"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E78.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle A_{0}^{\mathrm{PID}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>PID</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle A_{0}^{\mathrm{PID}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E78.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-a(i_{max}\!-\!1)\,{\bm{e}}_{v}(i_{max}\!-\!1)+b(i_{max}\!-\!1)\,{\bm{s}}_{v}(i_{max}\!-\!1)+c(i_{max}\!-\!1)\,\Delta{\bm{e}}_{v}(i_{max}\!-\!1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-a(i_{max}\!-\!1)\,{\bm{e}}_{v}(i_{max}\!-\!1)+b(i_{max}\!-\!1)\,{\bm{s}}_{v}(i_{max}\!-\!1)+c(i_{max}\!-\!1)\,\Delta{\bm{e}}_{v}(i_{max}\!-\!1)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(78)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E79"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E79.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-{\bm{w}}_{v}^{\perp}(i_{max}\!-\!1)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>v</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-{\bm{w}}_{v}^{\perp}(i_{max}\!-\!1),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(79)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS2.p8.3" class="ltx_p">Due to the monotone decrease before this first largest overshooting condition stated in the previous part and the fact that <math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c(k)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c(k)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c(k_{0}\!-\!1)\,\Delta{\bm{e}}_{v}(k_{0}\!-\!1)&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c(k_{0}\!-\!1)\,\Delta{\bm{e}}_{v}(k_{0}\!-\!1)&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore,</p>
<table id="A2.E80" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E80.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{0}^{PID}\ \leq\ b(i_{max}-1)\,{\bm{s}}_{v}(i_{max}-1)\;-\;a(i_{max}-1)\,{\bm{e}}_{v}(i_{max}-1)\;-\;{\bm{w}}_{v}^{\perp}(i_{max}-1)\;=\;A_{0}^{PI}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>v</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{0}^{PID}\ \leq\ b(i_{max}-1)\,{\bm{s}}_{v}(i_{max}-1)\;-\;a(i_{max}-1)\,{\bm{e}}_{v}(i_{max}-1)\;-\;{\bm{w}}_{v}^{\perp}(i_{max}-1)\;=\;A_{0}^{PI}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(80)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS2.p8.4" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\square" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\square</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS2.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS2.p9.1" class="ltx_p">Remark <a href="#Thmremark4" title="Remark 4 (Pre-overshoot monotonic decrease of scalar errors) ‣ B.7.2 Overshooting under PID law of control ‣ B.7 PID Control ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Proofs ‣ Activation Steering with a Feedback Controller" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> is neccessary because monotonic decrease of <math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{v}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{v}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> before the first peak is both a key technical property for proving Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2 (PID reduces the first-overshoot amplitude) ‣ 4.2.2 PID Control ‣ 4.2 Stability of the Error Dynamics: Roles and Caveats of PI and PID Control ‣ 4 Theoretical Analysis of PID Steering ‣ Activation Steering with a Feedback Controller" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> and a desirable feature of PID control itself. Indeed, as noted by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">Åström &amp; Hägglund (1995a, p.70)</a></cite>, poorly tuned derivative gains may produce non-monotonicity, in which case reducing only the first overshoot does not translate into improved overall behavior.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Additional Experimental Results</h2>

<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>Qualitative Examples of Concept Steering</h3>

<div id="A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Fig. <a href="#A3.F7" title="Figure 7 ‣ C.1 Qualitative Examples of Concept Steering ‣ Appendix C Additional Experimental Results ‣ Activation Steering with a Feedback Controller" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> and <a href="#A3.F8" title="Figure 8 ‣ C.1 Qualitative Examples of Concept Steering ‣ Appendix C Additional Experimental Results ‣ Activation Steering with a Feedback Controller" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> show that varying the intervention strength <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> produces a smooth and controllable progression of stylistic traits in the generated images. At low strengths (<math id="A3.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\approx 0.2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>≈</mo><mn>0.2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\approx 0.2</annotation></semantics></math>), subtle cues emerge, such as faint neon accents for the <span id="A3.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">cyberpunk</span> style or mild metallic shading for <span id="A3.SS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">steampunk</span>, while the overall image remains close to the original prompt. At moderate strengths (<math id="A3.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\approx 0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>≈</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\approx 0.5</annotation></semantics></math>), stylistic features become more salient: cyberpunk generations exhibit vivid neon lighting and futuristic cityscapes, whereas steampunk outputs show prominent brass textures, gears, and industrial motifs. Importantly, in this regime, the central semantic content of the prompt (i.e. objects, entities, and spatial composition) is preserved with high fidelity. At high intervention strengths (<math id="A3.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\geq 0.8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0.8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\geq 0.8</annotation></semantics></math>), stylistic traits dominate the visual appearance, often saturating the scene with strong color palettes or dense textures, yet semantic alignment to the original prompt remains largely intact, indicating that the steering primarily affects style without eroding core content.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.F7" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.04309v1/figs/style_visualize_cyberpunk.png" id="A3.F7.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_portrait" style="aspect-ratio:548/768;" width="548" height="768" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 7: </span>concept <span id="A3.F7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">cyberpunk</span>.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A3.F8" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.04309v1/figs/style_visualize_steampunk.png" id="A3.F8.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_portrait" style="aspect-ratio:548/768;" width="548" height="768" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 8: </span>Concept <span id="A3.F8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">steampunk</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
